&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Trade Desk does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firm recruiters. Fees will not be paid in the event a candidate submitted by a recruiter without an agreement in place is hired; such resumes will be deemed the sole property of The Trade Desk. The Trade Desk is an equal opportunity employer. All aspects of employment will be based on merit, competence, performance, and business needs. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, marital status, age, national origin, ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic information, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, veteran status, or any other status protected under federal, state, or local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Equal Opportunity Employer, The Trade Desk is committed to creating an inclusive hiring experience where everyone has the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please reach out to us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- ----- request an accommodation or discuss any accessibility needs you may require to access our Company Website or navigate any part of the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you contact us, please include your preferred contact details and specify the nature of your accommodation request or questions. Any information you share will be handled confidentially and will not impact our hiring decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/thetradedesk/associate-trading-director-agency-manchester-or-leeds-based-475187","tags":["Trading"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792832123},{"slug":"gtm-systems-lead-old-street-142487","company_name":"Granola","title":"GTM Systems Lead","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're Team Granola 👋</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Granola is an AI-powered notepad for people in back-to-back meetings. What started as a better way to take notes has become a shared workspace that helps teams capture, organize, and act on what matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building a product people genuinely love and are fortunate to work with many of the world's most ambitious companies. As we continue to grow, we're looking for a GTM Systems Lead to build the systems and data foundation that Sales, CS and leadership run on.<br /></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring a GTM Systems Lead to own the technology behind Granola’s commercial team as we scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll design, build and run the systems our Sales and CS teams rely on. Our current stack has served us well, but it needs to evolve as the team grows. You’ll take responsibility for how the tools fit together, what we build versus buy, and how information flows between them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. You’ll set the direction of the stack <strong>and</strong> implement the technical changes that make it work. You’ll work closely with Sales, CS and Data, and report to the Head of RevOps. You won’t be limited to administering a CRM or building isolated automations: you’ll own how the whole system works.<br /></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design and evolve the GTM stack.</strong> Decide how our Sales and CS systems should fit together, what to build versus buy, and what to prioritise as we grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the technical architecture of our CRM, Attio.</strong> Shape its data model, objects, workflows and integrations. You’ll be hands-on with configuration, particularly early on, but routine admin won’t be the sole focus of the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and maintain integrations.</strong> Make data flow reliably across Attio and our wider toolset, including Apollo, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Cal.com">Cal.com</a>, Tally and Polytomic, and into the data systems used by the wider business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the wider toolset.</strong> Assess new tools and vendors, improve or replace what isn’t working, and make sure the stack is useful, reliable and cost-conscious.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find opportunities for automation and AI.</strong> Identify work that could be made easier for Sales and CS, and build or collaborate on solutions where they fit the priorities of the stack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep systems dependable.</strong> Troubleshoot problems, establish sensible governance and documentation, and partner with IT on access and security.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Understand how teams work.</strong> Get close to Sales and CS workflows so the systems you build solve real problems, not just technical ones.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing, building and owning systems used by a growing commercial team. Relevant hands-on experience matters more to us than a particular number of years or experience with a specific CRM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound judgement about system architecture, priorities and build-versus-buy decisions—and the ability to explain those decisions to non-technical colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical depth beyond administering tools: you’ve built integrations and are comfortable working with APIs, webhooks and code. Experience with SQL, Python or JavaScript would be useful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of CRM data models, routing, enrichment and the operational work needed to keep data flowing reliably.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A willingness to get into the weeds. You’re comfortable doing the implementation yourself while also thinking about how the stack should develop over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about AI-powered GTM workflows, with experience building them a plus rather than a prerequisite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, low-ego approach. You can work through messy requests with Sales, CS and Data, challenge assumptions constructively, and ship solutions people can use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to have used Attio or every tool in our stack. We’re more interested in what you’ve built, how you think about systems, and how you’d apply that experience here.</p></li></ul><h2>About the Opportunity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are living in the most exciting time for tool builders since Engelbart's demo in 1968 and we want to assemble the best crew to build this future together. Our compensation philosophy is to hire the best people in the market and pay them accordingly with salary, variable, and equity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lastly, we think amazing talent comes from all kinds of life journeys and experiences. If what is written above speaks to you, whether you look like a fit on paper or not, please reach out.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/granola/gtm-systems-lead-old-street-142487","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792831215},{"slug":"data-engineer-cardiff-121842","company_name":"Veezu","title":"Data Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role at Veezu:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Data Engineer, you'll build and maintain the data platform that powers reporting, analytics and data science across Veezu. Reporting into the Director of Data Engineering, you'll work hands-on with Microsoft Fabric, SQL, Python/PySpark and Power BI, bringing data in from our booking systems, databases and third-party APIs and shaping it into trusted, well-modelled datasets that the business relies on every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who are Veezu?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Veezu is the UK's fastest growing taxi and private hire technology business operating across hundreds of UK towns and cities. We are a tech-driven on-demand mobility service that supports our hyper-local communities, helping them thrive and so much more!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build and maintain ETL/ELT pipelines in Microsoft Fabric using Pipelines, Notebooks, Lakehouses, Warehouses and OneLake.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write PySpark notebooks to ingest and transform data from SQL Server databases, REST APIs, SaaS applications and file-based exports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and optimise SQL transformations, stored procedures and Kimball-style star-schema data models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and support Power BI semantic models and the datasets behind dashboards used by teams across the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement data quality, validation and reconciliation checks so numbers match across systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor production pipelines and troubleshoot data, performance and refresh issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Git, automated testing and CI/CD to support reliable, repeatable deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain clear documentation, data lineage and engineering standards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with analysts and business stakeholders to turn requirements into practical data solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be committed to maintaining our ISO27001 certification and set high standards for Information Security compliance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll need:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-4 years' experience in a data engineering role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong SQL skills, including complex transformations and performance tuning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with Microsoft Fabric (or Azure Synapse / Data Factory and a willingness to move to Fabric).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python and PySpark for data ingestion and transformation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating data from APIs and other external sources.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good knowledge of data warehousing and dimensional modelling (Kimball).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Power BI and semantic models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of data quality, testing and reconciliation, and experience with Git / source control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence communicating with technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CI/CD and automated testing for data pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Microsoft Fabric certification (e.g. DP-600 or DP-700).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lakehouse / medallion architecture design patterns.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with data governance, security and lineage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high-volume transactional data, ideally in transport, mobility or on-demand services.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Where you’ll be:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is hybrid, based out of our Cardiff HQ, with 3 days per week in the office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Veezu is committed to fair and inclusive recruitment, welcoming applications from all backgrounds, experiences, and communities.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/veezu/data-engineer-cardiff-121842","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Cardiff HQ","created_at":1792831215},{"slug":"senior-account-executive-manchester-186832","company_name":"Cytix","title":"Senior Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Senior Account Executive to own full-cycle new-logo revenue for Cytix's biggest and most complex deals, in a market where most of the people you're calling haven't heard of us yet. You'll be selling a product, not a service, into CISOs, security engineers and AppSec leads who are used to being pitched by categories they already understand. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your job is to earn a conversation with almost no brand recognition behind you, then run a genuinely consultative sale that gets underneath what a prospect is actually trying to achieve, not just what they say they want.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll take on enterprise and partner-adjacent opportunities, competitive procurement, and buying groups that span security, engineering and the economic buyer. You'll also set the bar for the wider sales team: shaping how SDR intake and Customer Success handoff work, and helping newer Account Executives find their feet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own full-cycle new-logo opportunities from first qualified meeting through discovery, technical evaluation and signature, sourced by SDR, Marketing, partners and your own prospecting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-source a meaningful share of your own pipeline; build an account plan from a cold list rather than relying on inbound or SDR support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run multi-threaded discovery across security, engineering and economic buyers, uncovering pain that a single conversation would miss.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own commercial negotiation, procurement and security review through to signature, including competitive processes, without needing support from the CRO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain an accurate weekly forecast, with commit-to-close accuracy within 10%, sustained over multiple quarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape SDR intake criteria and the Customer Success handoff standard; informally mentor newer Account Executives on deal strategy and technical positioning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hand off cleanly to Customer Success at close, with deal-stage commitments documented in the CRM.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–7+ years' full-cycle closing experience in B2B SaaS, ideally selling a technical product, not a service, into security or engineering buyers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A demonstrable track record of carrying and hitting quota of £750k–£1m+, at or above 100% in at least two of the last three years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuine consultative selling skill: </strong>comfortable asking why before pitching how, and building a business case from first principles rather than a script.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence selling into accounts where Cytix has little or no existing brand presence, building credibility through the conversation itself rather than a logo slide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of pushing through setbacks and coming back stronger, and of actively seeking out the harder, less familiar deals rather than waiting to be asked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuinely bright and inquisitive: </strong>you ask sharp questions, pick things up fast, and enjoy getting to the bottom of a problem, whether that's a prospect's business or how Cytix's product works under the hood.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drawn to a business where new challenges show up daily; you take ownership of them and lean in, rather than waiting for someone else to sort it out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable taking yourself out of your comfort zone: </strong>new deal types, new buyer personas, situations you haven't fully rehearsed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll get</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off that works for you: Unlimited holiday policy, including a guaranteed 33 days plus your birthday off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible hybrid working: Work in a way that helps you do your best work, while staying connected with the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A stake in what we’re building: Eligible employees can participate in our EMI share option scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthcare that goes further: After one year’s service, access private healthcare through Vitality, including dental, optical, hearing and therapy cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">More ways to get around: Access our company car salary-sacrifice scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support for growing families: Enhanced maternity and paternity leave.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Cytix</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software never stops changing. Teams ship new code every day, through tickets, pull requests, releases, and increasingly with AI in the mix, but the way security keeps up with all that change hasn't really moved on. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's the problem we're solving. Cytix helps organisations understand which software changes actually matter, what should happen next, and how to prove the right call was made. Security understood, in other words.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a small team with big plans, so every person we hire genuinely shapes what Cytix becomes. That's why we're upfront about our five values: we interview for all of them, and they matter to us more than a perfect CV. They're things you do, not things you are, so have a read and see if they sound like you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make the first move.</strong> When the goal is clear but the path isn't, you get moving rather than waiting for perfect instructions. If you're blocked, you make a sensible call, say what you're assuming, and explain how you'd course-correct. We'd rather you act and be slightly wrong than sit still.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find the smarter path.</strong> You ask why before how. You dig into what the real problem is instead of just building what the spec says, and you're happy to question 'that's how it's always been done' when the reason behind it has gone stale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>See it through.</strong> When something's yours, it lands. No loose ends, no surprises for whoever picks it up next. You keep people posted when things change, and if something falls between roles, you catch it.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Raise the bar.</strong> You do the best job possible in the time you've got, whether that's a day or a month. Sometimes that means deep craft; sometimes the smartest move is quick and scrappy. It's about good judgement, and we hold each other to it without blame or politics.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to win.</strong> You care about the mission but don't take yourself too seriously. You say 'I' when things go wrong and 'we' when they go right, trust teammates to do things their own way, and bring a bit of humour when the pressure's on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £75K – £95K • OTE - uncapped 50/50</p><ul><li> • £75K – £95K • OTE - uncapped 50/50</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cytix/senior-account-executive-manchester-186832","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Manchester","created_at":1792831215},{"slug":"people-operations-specialist-london-133973","company_name":"Legora","title":"People Operations Specialist","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Few companies at this stage have this much to design and build at once, and at scale! Rapid geographic expansion and the establishment of multiple legal entities place demands on our People function to keep pace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>People Operations Specialist</strong>, you'll execute and continuously improve the operational processes that power every stage of the employee lifecycle as we grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to the People Operations &amp; People Program Lead, you'll work hands-on across Legora's core People function, partnering closely with People Partners, People Tech, Payroll, Legal and Finance. Our mission is to build operational excellence that enables the business to scale without creating unnecessary complexity.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute and continuously improve core People Operations processes across the entire employee lifecycle with speed, accuracy and attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the day-to-day administration of onboarding, offboarding, employee changes, promotions, transfers, leave processes and organisational updates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare documentation and employee records, ensuring every process is completed accurately and on time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain high-quality employee data and ensure operational accuracy across all People processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, document and maintain scalable operating procedures, playbooks and process documentation that enable consistent execution globally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate People Operations activities across multiple stakeholders, countries and time zones, ensuring nothing falls through the cracks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify manual work, operational inefficiencies and recurring issues, and propose and implement better ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with People Tech to improve operational workflows and prepare processes for automation, while leaving technical implementation to the People Tech team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support international expansion, acquisitions and organisational changes by executing operational People processes at pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help establish operational metrics, monitor service quality and continuously raise the bar for operational excellence.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in People Operations, HR Operations or HR Administration in a fast-growing company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional attention to detail — you genuinely enjoy getting the operational details right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong administrative skills, with experience managing large volumes of employee lifecycle activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with HR systems as a power user (rather than as a system administrator).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organised, with excellent prioritisation skills and the ability to manage multiple deadlines simultaneously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in an environment where priorities change quickly, without compromising quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A continuous improvement mindset — you naturally look for ways to simplify, standardise and improve operational processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong written documentation skills and the ability to create clear, repeatable operational procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working independently, with a high degree of ownership and accountability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building agents/agentic workflows as part of People processes is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legor