 a real impact, and the challenge of selling category-defining technology, we want to hear from you. You'll be selling solutions that fundamentally change how enterprises operate, working with executive buyers who are making multi-million dollar, multi-year commitments to AI transformation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hybrid role based out of our London hub. You'll be reporting to our regional vice president.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🦸🏻‍♀️ What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full enterprise sales cycle from prospecting through close, managing complex deals with 8-18 month sales cycles and navigating multi-stakeholder buying committees across procurement, legal, IT, and business units</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive net-new revenue by identifying, qualifying, and developing strategic opportunities within target verticals and named account lists, consistently building a robust pipeline that exceeds coverage targets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage C-level executives and senior decision-makers in consultative discovery to understand their business priorities, uncover transformational use cases, and position WRITER as the strategic platform to achieve their AI vision</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner cross-functionally with solutions engineering, product, and customer success teams to architect tailored solutions, run successful pilots, and ensure seamless deployments that deliver measurable business outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead complex negotiations involving multi-year contracts, custom pricing structures, and enterprise terms, while maintaining deal momentum and driving consensus across diverse stakeholder groups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Become a trusted product expert who educates prospects on how to set up and leverage WRITER's AI agent platform, going hands-on during critical evaluation phases to demonstrate value and accelerate time-to-deployment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain rigorous pipeline hygiene and forecasting accuracy, consistently delivering predictable revenue results while providing leadership with transparent visibility into deal progression and risk factors</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⭐️ What you need</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7-10+ years of quota-carrying strategic SaaS sales experience with a proven track record of meeting or exceeding annual quotas in complex, value-based sales motions targeting Fortune 500 and Global 2000 accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated expertise in managing sophisticated enterprise sales cycles with multiple stakeholders, navigating procurement processes, and orchestrating cross-functional resources to drive deals through technical evaluations and executive approvals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive presence and communication skills that allow you to credibly engage with C-suite buyers (CIOs, CDOs, CTOs, COOs), translate complex technical concepts into business value, and build authentic relationships based on trust and strategic insight</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong consultative selling skills with the ability to conduct discovery that uncovers underlying business challenges, connects AI capabilities to measurable outcomes, and creates urgency around transformation initiatives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in outbound prospecting, account mapping, and territory planning, with a hunter mentality that drives you to consistently create new opportunities rather than waiting for inbound leads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguity and a bias for ownership – you thrive in fast-paced environments where you're expected to figure things out, make decisions with incomplete infor