&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Account Executive – SAP Ecosystem &amp;amp; Digital Transformation for Benelux&amp;nbsp; &amp;amp; Nordics (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Enterprise Account Executive, reporting to VP of Global GTM .We are seeking an elite, high-performing &lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt; to drive new business acquisition across top-tier accounts. Combining large-enterprise sophistication with an aggressive, entrepreneurial hunting mindset, you will architect transformational security deals, engage C-level stakeholders, and position &lt;strong&gt;business resilience&lt;/strong&gt; for the world’s most mission-critical ERP environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Strategic Revenue:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the full sales lifecycle for Global 2000 accounts, positioning the Onapsis Platform as the essential security layer for SAP and Business Critical Applications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The SAP &quot;Triple Threat&quot;:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Sales:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage complex, high-value &quot;land and expand&quot; cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SAP Co-Sell:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with SAP Account Executives (AEs) and Enterprise Architects&amp;nbsp; to attach Onapsis to S/4HANA and RISE migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GSI Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrate go-to-market strategies with Global Systems Integrators (Accenture, Deloitte, IBM, PwC) who are leading the world&#39;s largest SAP transformations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C-Suite Advisory:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a trusted advisor to CISOs and CIOs, translating technical vulnerabilities into business risks (e.g., SOX compliance, financial downtime, and data integrity).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute an annual territory plan focused on &quot;White Space&quot; analysis within the SAP installed base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecast Accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a high level of &quot;Sales Hygiene&quot; within CRM, delivering predictable weekly and monthly forecasts aligned with SAP’s rigorous reporting standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills/Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Enterprise Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 7–10+ years of enterprise software sales experience, with a proven history of selling complex software solutions within the SAP ecosystem (either at SAP or a top-tier partner).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Transformation Expert:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of the &lt;strong&gt;RISE with SAP&lt;/strong&gt; framework, &lt;strong&gt;Clean Core&lt;/strong&gt; strategy, and the &lt;strong&gt;SAP Business Technology Platform (BTP)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consistent High Achiever:&lt;/strong&gt; Consistent record of quota over-achievement, regularly closing seven-figure ARR deals across Global 2000 accounts with complex buying committees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alliance Savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success in &quot;partner-first&quot; selling, particularly with GSIs and SAP’s regional field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional executive presence; ability to move seamlessly from a technical discussion with a Basis Lead to a strategic ROI pitch with a CFO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to travel: &lt;/strong&gt;We believe that our business is a people business and that trust is built in person. Between 25-50% travel required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entrepreneurial Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Proactive self-starter with the drive to build a territory from scratch and take full ownership of business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language: &lt;/strong&gt;Professional fluency in English. Additional regional language skills are a strong plus (written and spoken).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can expect a job with responsible tasks and creative opportunities, and an attractive salary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have flexible working hours with us. In addition, you can work remotely from other EU countries by arrangement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in a late-stage, high-growth leader backed by top-tier VC/PE firms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to represent the only cybersecurity solution endorsed by SAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Furthermore, you can expect an innovative and attractive workplace with flat hierarchies and respectful and solution-oriented communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Onapsis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onapsis protects the business applications that run the global economy. The Onapsis Platform delivers vulnerability management, change assurance, and continuous compliance for business applications from leading vendors such as SAP, Oracle, and others. The Onapsis Platform is powered by the Onapsis Research Labs, the team responsible for the discovery and mitigation of more than 1,000 zero-day vulnerabilities in business applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onapsis is headquartered in Boston, MA, with offices in Dallas, TX, Heidelberg, Germany, Bucharest, Romania, and Buenos Aires, Argentina, and proudly serves hundreds of the world’s leading brands, including close to 30% of the Forbes Global 100, six of the top 10 automotive companies, five of the top 10 chemical companies, four of the top 10 technology companies, and three of the top 10 oil and gas companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/onapsis/enterprise-account-executive-sap-ecosystem-digital-transformation-for-benelux-nordics-london-211272","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792821319},{"slug":"senior-product-marketing-manager-uk-remote-109523","company_name":"grafanalabs","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager  | UK | Remote","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an enthusiastic, tech-forward product marketer to grow our Observability products by boldly positioning them and running campaigns to attract, convert and retain customers. As a Senior Product Marketing Manager, you will be in charge of the messaging and positioning for a broad product area. Then you’ll work closely with product managers and the marketing team to deliver campaigns, content, events, and training that help buyers buy (and sellers sell) our value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Marketing lives within the Product org rather than the Marketing org at Grafana Labs, and we think differently about the job. Rather than purely executing launches or campaigns, we want PMMs to teach product managers and engineers in our org how to think about growth and demand, and to codify product marketing knowledge into AI-forward tools and processes that anyone in the organization can use. For example, we all contribute product information to a shared knowledge base, which we use to generate enablement materials and decks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is a fast-paced and growing organization. As such, this role requires strategic skills, an interest in teaching, and hands-on tactical execution (blogs, webinar outlines, video scripts, etc). Our team is full of people who crave impact and independence - if you are seeking a role with narrow scope where you run a defined playbook, this is not the job for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively partner with and teach product managers to define product value, messaging, and go-to-market strategy, from competitive positioning to sales enablement collateral.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product management, engineering and various go-to-market functions to create materials that help customers evaluate and adopt our products: reference architectures, implementation guides, detailed product information and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer lifecycle campaigns (competitive positioning, retention, upsell/cross-sell) to strategically shape marketing programs and drive growth across the entire customer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market and customer research to understand pain points, competition and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach go-to-market and sales teams our products’ capabilities and the value they provide, deliver training and enablement, ensure customer facing teams are able to effectively engage with customers, partners, and prospects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant experience (product marketing, solutions marketing, product management)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketing and selling to a technical audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for open source, cloud native, and infrastructure technologies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to take on complex projects and efficiently drive them from start to finish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly articulate the value of technical products to customers and sellers alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading product or feature launches autonomously as well as part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with AI tools like ChatGPT and Claude to automate messaging and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with a variety of internal and external stakeholders in complicated processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product and technical curiosity that translate to clear packaging, positioning, and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated quantitative analytical skills for analyzing campaign performance, evaluating lifecycle metrics, and making data-driven recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high “say-do” ratio in executing and delivering impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the UK, the base compensation range for this role is GBP 91,755 - GBP 110,106. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;*Compensation ranges are country specific. If you are applying for this role from a different location than listed above, your recruiter will discuss your specific market’s defined pay range &amp;amp; benefits at the beginning of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Thrive at Grafana Labs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;100% Remote, Global Culture -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;As a remote-only company, we bring together talent from around the world, united by a culture of collaboration and shared purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling Organization&lt;/strong&gt; – Tackle meaningful work in a high-growth, ever-evolving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparent Communication&lt;/strong&gt; – Expect open decision-making and regular company-wide updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation-Driven&lt;/strong&gt; – Autonomy and support to ship great work and try new things.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Source Roots&lt;/strong&gt; – Built on community-driven values that shape how we work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empowered Teams&lt;/strong&gt; – High trust, low ego culture that values outcomes over optics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career Growth Pathways&lt;/strong&gt; – Defined opportunities to grow and develop your career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approachable Leadership&lt;/strong&gt; – Transparent execs who are involved, visible, and human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Passionate People&lt;/strong&gt; – Join a team of smart, supportive folks who care deeply about what they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Person onboarding &lt;/strong&gt;- We want you to thrive from day 1 with your fellow new ‘Grafanistas’ to learn all about what we do and how we do it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balance is Key&lt;/strong&gt; - We operate a global annual leave policy of 30 days per annum. 3 days of your annual leave entitlement are reserved for Grafana Shutdown Days to allow the team to really disconnect. &lt;em&gt;*We will comply with local legislation where applicable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Grafana Labs is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from everyone regardless of race, colour, nationality, origin, caste, sex, gender reassignment identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, religion or belief, disability, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, maternity, marital, family or carer status, or any other characteristic which is protected by local law. We believe that equality and diversity build a strong organisation, and we work hard to ensure that is the foundation of our organisation as we grow.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Grafana Labs may utilize AI tools in its recruitment process to assist in matching information provided in CVs to job postings. The recruitment team will continue to review inbound CVs manually to identify alignment with current openings.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;For information about how your personal data is used once you’ve applied to a job, check out our &lt;a href=&quot;https://grafana.com/legal/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;privacy policy&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/grafanalabs/senior-product-marketing-manager-uk-remote-109523","tags":["Product"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792821319},{"slug":"principal-technical-marketing-engineer-uk-remote-443727","company_name":"grafanalabs","title":"Principal Technical Marketing Engineer  | UK | Remote","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is the company behind Grafana Cloud, the fully managed observability platform trusted by more than 10,000 organizations to ensure reliability, resolve incidents faster, and optimize telemetry at scale. Built on open source and open standards and designed for interoperability across any stack, Grafana Cloud brings AI to observability and observability to AI, giving teams (and their agents) unified visibility so they can see, understand, and act on all their disparate data, wherever it lives, and move at the speed of their ambitions. Customers, including Anthropic, Bloomberg, NVIDIA, Microsoft, and Salesforce, rely on Grafana Labs. We are a 100% remote company with team members across 40+ countries, backed by leading investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Sequoia Capital, GIC, Coatue, J.P. Morgan, CapitalG, and Lead Edge Capital. Learn more at &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://grafana.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;grafana.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and follow us on &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/grafana-labs/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;u&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/grafana&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is looking for a technically fluent engineer who loves building powerful demos, explaining complex systems clearly, and helping SRE and platform engineering leaders understand the value of our open approach to observability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Grafana’s offering shifts from dashboards to industry-leading agentic observability, our Product Marketing team is responsible for closing the gap between what our products can do and how customers understand that value. That means building clear, consistent positioning, enabling sellers with trustworthy technical narratives, and creating content that helps Platform Engineering teams quickly grasp why Grafana Cloud is the right choice for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Product Marketer you will play a critical part in that transformation. You’ll be the hands-on engineer who brings our technical story to life for buyers, not just practitioners. You’ll build core demos, run technical workshops and webinars, and act as the technical bridge between our Product and Sales orgs. Your work will help SRE and platform engineering leaders evaluate Grafana with confidence, equip sales engineers with better tools and talk tracks, and ensure our technical value shows up clearly and consistently across the entire customer journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique chance to shape how Grafana tells its story as we evolve our positioning in the AI era, strengthen seller enablement, and build a repeatable system for communicating product value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build strategic, buyer-focused demos, videos, workshops, and webinars&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain polished, narrative-driven demos that highlight Grafana’s value for SRE and platform engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record high-quality technical demo videos and walkthroughs in partnership with our video and content teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead webinars, workshops, and technical sessions designed for evaluators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach customers not just how Grafana works, but why our approach is differentiated and valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to generate variations, summaries, and reusable assets that scale technical content across channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable Solutions (Sales) Engineers with clear, consistent technical storytelling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as PMM’s technical liaison to the SE org, ensuring consistent messaging and demo guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce technical enablement assets, value-driven talk tracks, competitive narratives, and demo best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help SEs and sellers communicate Grafana’s story with clarity, confidence, and differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with PMMs to drive technical buyer engagement across high-impact channels&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with PMMs to identify the most important buyer personas, problems, and technical messages, and help shape the content strategy needed to reach them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend technical narratives into impactful buyer-facing channels including analyst briefings (Gartner, Forrester), industry forums, podcasts, conferences, and online technical communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a technical perspective to PMM planning—helping ensure our content, campaigns, and enablement reflect the real challenges and priorities of SREs and engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use automation &amp;amp; AI to scale technical content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with software engineers to streamline demo setup, content workflows, and asset updates through workflows, agents, scripts, and AI-driven tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use automation to make technical content more repeatable, discoverable, and scalable across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a technical role (solutions engineering, SRE, DevOps, backend engineering, technical PMM, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and ability to travel to training and customer events 10-12 weeks per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of observability concepts and the needs of SRE/platform teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate deep technical concepts into clear, value-focused stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting technical content through demos, workshops, or webinars.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with a crisp, structured, persuasive style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration; comfort working with PMM, Product, SEs, DevRel, and Field Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership mindset with the ability to drive projects from concept to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with light scripting or workflow automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Grafana, Prometheus, Loki, Mimir, Tempo, or similar observability tools, or a background in Observability or Platform Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in Sales Engineering, DevRel, or technical product marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with demo environment automation or infrastructure-as-code tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional live presentation or workshop facilitation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the UK, the base compensation range for this role is GBP &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;103,958&lt;/span&gt;- GBP &lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;124,750&lt;/span&gt;. Actual compensation may vary based on level, experience, and skillset as assessed throughout the interview process. All of our roles include Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), giving every team member ownership in Grafana Labs&#39; success. We believe in shared outcomes—RSUs help us stay aligned and invested as we scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
