gineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1792821316},{"slug":"senior-frontend-engineer-london-53961","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Senior Frontend Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;">We are seeking a talented&nbsp;<strong>Front End Engineer</strong>&nbsp;with over 5 years of professional experience to join our new UK team. You will be responsible for building sleek, responsive, and user-friendly interfaces to enable real-time control and monitoring of robotic swarms and sensor systems. Your work will directly contribute to the usability and efficiency of our cutting-edge robotics solutions.</p><p style="text-align:justify;"><br></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Design, develop, and optimize frontend applications for controlling and visualizing robotic swarms and sensor data.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with backend engineers to integrate APIs and ensure seamless data flow between frontend and backend systems.</p></li><li><p>Build intuitive, performant, and responsive user interfaces using modern frontend frameworks such as React or comparable web component frameworks.</p></li><li><p>Work closely with UX/UI designers to translate designs into functional applications.</p></li><li><p>Ensure code quality, maintainability, and scalability through clean coding practices and code reviews.</p></li><li><p>Troubleshoot and optimize frontend performance for real-time applications.</p></li></ul> <br> <p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>5+ years of professional experience in frontend development.</p></li><li><p>Proficiency in&nbsp;<strong>TypeScript</strong>&nbsp;and web component frameworks.</p></li><li><p>Strong understanding of modern web development tools, concepts, and practices.</p></li><li><p>Basic knowledge of backend systems and API integration.</p></li><li><p>Experience with custom web-based rendering engines</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with RESTful APIs, WebSockets, and data visualization tools.</p></li><li><p>Ability to write clean, efficient, and well-documented code.</p></li><li><p>Excellent problem-solving skills and a passion for building user-friendly applications</p></li></ul><p><strong>Nice-to-Have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience with robotics, sensor data visualization, or real-time control systems.</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of state management libraries (e.g., Redux, MobX) and frontend build tools.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with backend technologies such as <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Node.js">Node.js</a> or similar.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of testing frameworks and tools for front-end development.</p></li></ul><h4></h4><p><br></p><h4><strong>Why Quantum-Systems:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>We believe in the power of combined&nbsp;efforts: straightforward tech expertise&nbsp;paired with a customer-centric focus.</p></li><li><p>We are industry pioneers&nbsp;who are ambitious, bold,&nbsp;and visionary. </p></li><li><p>We push limits, think&nbsp;outside-the-box and strive&nbsp;for technological excellence to&nbsp;shape the future of aerial data.</p></li><li><p>We promise to be your runway&nbsp;for individual and professional&nbsp;growth.</p></li></ul><p><strong><br></strong></p><h4><strong>Our benefits:</strong></h4><ul><li><p><strong>Company pension scheme: </strong>We support you so that you can already make provisions for later.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexible working hours: </strong>With trust-based working hours, you are not only responsible for your working hours, but also for your work-life balance.</p></li><li><p><strong>Mobile working: </strong>If it gets too turbulent for you in our office, you can get the necessary balance through mobile working.</p></li><li><p><strong>Bike-Leasing: </strong>We support you in staying environmentally mobile and healthy.</p></li><li><p><strong>Corporate Benefits: </strong>Your opportunity for attractive offers and discounts from well-known suppliers and brands, e.g. Adidas, Apple, Expedia.</p></li><li><p><strong>Employee events: </strong>We not only want to grow together, but also celebrate our successes together.</p></li></ul><p><br></p><h4><strong>About us:</strong></h4><p style="text-align:justify;">Quantum Systems specialises in the development, design, and production of small Unmanned Aerial Systems (sUAS). The company’s range of electric vertical take-off and landing (eVTOL) sUAS are built to maximize range and versatility and to provide operators with a seamless user experience. By integrating cutting-edge software capabilities, like edge computing and real-time AI-powered data processing, Quantum Systems is building next-generation UAS for clients in defence, security, public sectors.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><iframe height="281" width="500" src="//www.youtube.com/embed/_tjzWB0ttBM"></iframe></figure><p><br></p><h4><strong>Our commitment:</strong></h4><p>We are an open-minded company that not only values diversity, but actively promotes it. Regardless of gender, age, ethnic origin, religion, sexual orientation or disability, we firmly believe that the diversity of our employees is an essential part of our success.</p><p>At our company, every voice is heard and every perspective is valued. We believe that our differences enrich us and help us to find creative solutions and generate innovative ideas. We pride ourselves on creating an inclusive work environment where all employees can reach their full potential.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/quantum-systems-gmbh/senior-frontend-engineer-london-53961","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792821098},{"slug":"senior-av-technician-london-336107","company_name":"Kinly","title":"Senior AV Technician","description":"<figure><img style="width:452px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/fo55ugu51dch1w8gbylfbmy5omekr7/Logo.jpg"></figure><p class="MsoNormal">Role:&nbsp;<strong>Senior</strong> <strong>AV Technician</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Contract Type:&nbsp;<strong>Full-time, Permanent</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Hours:<strong> Shift pattern based upon a 40hr working week between the hours of 07:00 &amp; 19:00 ensuring coverage throughout the period, some flexibility may, on occasion, be required</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Location:&nbsp;<strong>London, UK (Canary Wharf)</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Salary:&nbsp;<strong>£44,000 - £50,000 (dependent on experience), plus company benefits</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Interview Process: <strong>2-stage (Virtual and Face-to-face)</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">Kinly is a leading integrator of audio-visual and unified communications solutions, and the largest in Europe, serving as a globally trusted technology advisor to leading organisations. For more than 25 years, we have been designing, developing, integrating and supporting complex audiovisual solutions and businesses rely on us to deliver consistently secure and flexible meeting experiences.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">We have an exciting new client; a company that is globally renowned operating within the financial services industry and they are now looking to recruit a proven AV Technician onto their impressive site in Canary Wharf to provide dedicated support services to the AV technology estate.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">The team proactively maintain and monitor AV (from meeting rooms, digital signage, specialist spaces) to minimise downtime and ensure excellent customer service &amp; experience and undertake functionality tests of high-priority spaces, and ad-hoc and pro-active AV maintenance, technical problem solving, support and occasional small upgrade installation work.</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Key responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Perform daily checks of critical digital signage, including the external ticker, reception LED wall, internal display areas, and booth signage where applicable</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Fault finding audio visual and video conferencing systems to a high level, under pressure</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Work collaboratively on troubleshooting and fault fixing</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Maintaining site surveys and asset registers</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Running AV events, including pre-event testing of audio, wireless microphone battery levels, PA, projector/display, conferencing, and post-event reset support etc.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Be the primary contact for event coordination</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Liaise with client for large events to understand their requirements</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Attend pre-production meetings required for any scheduled special events</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Primary support to operate global production events</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Own the event experiences for the meeting host and attendees</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Assist in the management of high-profile events and become a trusted advisor</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Escalate any operational issues to the appropriate level of support and make suggestions for improvements</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Produce event reports which highlight the use of space</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Skills and experience:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Knowledge of collaboration platforms such as Polycom, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Google</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Ability to operate Videoconference hardware (Microsoft Teams, Webex, Poly, Logi etc) and to troubleshoot any potential issues relating to audio feedback, no video etc.</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Proficiency with Microsoft Teams, UC PCs, Polycom, Logitech, and Crestron</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Flex VC solutions, Biamp&nbsp;&nbsp; Tesira, Q-SYS, and Extron</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experience in supporting IPTV</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Experienced delivering support services to large corporate customers</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Excellent people skills with the ability to impart knowledge to those less skilled</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Expected to complete security screening (BPSS &amp; SC) which will be subject to employment</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;"><strong>If you are selected for interview, and need any reasonable adjustments made for your interview, please let the Talent Acquisition team know, at the point of scheduling.</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:center;"><strong>If you do require details of the vacancy or the application process in an alternative format, please email&nbsp;<u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- your requirements.</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Equal Opportunities:</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Kinly is committed to providing equal opportunities in employment, all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, age, gender identity, pregnancy, colour, race, national origin, sexual orientation, disability, religion or any other ‘protected characteristics. We welcome your application.</p><figure><img style="width:1152px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/8m1dpupdvefdupydphotbsmgs6ekg4/Brand_Values_White_no_title_long.png"></figure> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kinly/senior-av-technician-london-336107","tags":["United Kingdom"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, England, United Kingdom","created_at":1792821098},{"slug":"intelligence-origination-senior-credit-reporter-london-6039","company_name":"Gain","title":"Intelligence Origination – (Senior) Credit Reporter","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who Are We?</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Gain is the Private Markets Super App, a connected global platform transforming how leading investors, advisors, and corporates source, evaluate, and execute deals. By combining investment-grade intelligence, AI-powered workflows, and proprietary data in one unified platform, Gain enables top deal teams to move faster, reduce risk, and build conviction with confidence.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Gain is trusted across more than $1 trillion of private capital, used by 100% of MBB and Big Four firms, and by 80% of the world’s top 20 M&amp;A advisory houses.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Recognized for fast innovation and impact, Gain has been named both US and EU Data Provider of the Year by PE Wire, awarded Global Financial Market Review’s Best Use of AI in Finance, and ranked in Sifted’s Top 100 Fastest-Growing Companies, the Forbes 1000, and the Deloitte Technology Fast 50. Gain operates globally with offices in New York, London, Amsterdam, Frankfurt, Warsaw, and Bangalore.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What will you do?</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">We are expanding our Intelligence Origination team into Credit. This team is responsible for sourcing proprietary, transaction-level credit intelligence across live and announced private equity-related transactions. Unlike traditional newsrooms, our model is data-first, capturing structured intelligence rather than producing news stories.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">You will play a pivotal role in expanding our real-time credit intelligence coverage. The focus is on the completeness, accuracy and speed of data capture - not editorial output. Your mission is to cultivate a trusted network of off-record sources, including lenders, investment bankers, private equity sponsors, advisors, consultants and lawyers, to uncover proprietary market intelligence.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">The insights you gather will be transformed into clean, machine-readable data that powers our platform and forms the backbone of our clients' origination and transaction analysis workflows.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">You'll speak with market participants on a background-only basis, surfacing intelligence that rarely enters the public domain. Working closely with our analysts and research teams, you'll help convert raw market insight into structured, scalable data that fuels client workflows and supports better investment decisions.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Key Responsibilities:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">In your role, you will:</span></p><ul><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Build and maintain a network of sources - including lenders, investment bankers, sponsors, advisors and lawyers</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Conduct daily off-record, high-trust conversations to surface non-public credit intelligence</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Ensure high-quality sourcing of proprietary datapoints that feed directly into the Gain platform&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Collaborate closely with our in-house analysts and research teams to ensure data completeness, consistency and structured format</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Support the expansion of our real-time transaction tracker and contribute to internal market intelligence sharing</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who are you?</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You have:</span></p><ul><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">2–4 years of relevant professional experience and strong knowledge of private credit, leveraged finance, M&amp;A, private equity, restructuring, or a related field</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Experience sourcing market intelligence - in journalism, research, origination, investor relations or a related field</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">A background in covering deals in private credit, distressed debt/restructuring, high-yield bond and leveraged loan offerings is preferred but not necessarily essential</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Skilled at cultivating senior-level sources and handling off-record, background-only conversations</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, both in-person and remotely</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">High attention to detail and ability to work quickly without sacrificing accuracy</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Comfortable operating independently as part of a fast-moving, entrepreneurial team</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">What do we offer? </span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">base salary </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">and </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">annual bonus</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> linked to your performance</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Attractive benefits</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> including private medical insurance, health &amp; wellbeing allowance, work-from-home budget, learning &amp; coaching benefits, etc.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Flexible hybrid working model </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">with 3 days per week in our London office</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Healthy </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">work-life balance</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> allowing for planability and personal commitments</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Chance to </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">grow with the company</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> gaining increasing responsibilities, supported by lots of coaching and a feedback-driven approach</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Tremendous learning</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> and </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">career progression </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">opportunities</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">International environment </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">with hubs in New York, Amsterdam, London, Frankfurt, Warsaw, and Bangalore</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Culture of </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">trust, ownership and standard of excellence</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> and</span><strong><span style="color:#000000"> fun working atmosphere</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> with regular outings and events</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Post product-market fit </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">and aspiring unicorn status - this is an excellent time to </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">join &amp; grow with us</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">!</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Does this sound like a perfect match?</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">We are proud of our wonderful product and believe it has lots of potential. We are growing fast and having fun while building our platform and company. Does this sound like a team you would like to become a part of? We are excited to get to know you and show you what we do!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Gain.AI"><span style="color:#000000">Gain.AI</span></a><em><span style="color:#000000"> B.V., with its registered seat in Apollolaan 151, 1077 AR Amsterdam, The Netherlands, or another </span></em><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Gain.AI"><span style="color:#000000">Gain.AI</span></a><em><span style="color:#000000"> or </span></em><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Gain.pro"><span style="color:#000000">Gain.pro</span></a><em><span style="color:#000000"> entity which runs the recruitment process, further called „Gain", is the controller of personal data you submit as part of the job application. Your personal data will be processed for the purpose of conducting a recruitment process for the job position you apply for. If you provide Gain with explicit consent, your personal data will also be processed for the purpose of conducting future recruitment processes. Please read the Gain Privacy Policy to acquaint yourself with how Gain processes your personal data: </span></em><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.gain.ai/privacy-and-cookie-statement."><span style="color:#000000">https://www.gain.ai/privacy-and-cookie-statement.</span></a></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><em><span style="color:#000000">Gain is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/gain/intelligence-origination-senior-credit-reporter-london-6039","tags":["Private Equity Intelligence"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792821095},{"slug":"large-loss-claims-handler-halifax-uk-163248","company_name":"Zego","title":"Large Loss Claims Handler","description":"<h2><strong>About Zego 🚀</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Zego, we're on a mission to do the good thing, not the insurance thing.<br /><br />Insurance hasn't changed much in over a century. The way we live, work and travel has. We're building the real-time, AI-driven infrastructure that powers innovative insurance, so good drivers get cover that works the way they actually drive.<br /><br /><strong>We're not just updating insurance; We're leading the AI evolution in insurance </strong>🤖</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For us, AI isn't a line on a roadmap or a buzzword on a slide. It's our operating reality, and it's how we build products that back drivers instead of the old insurance playbook.<br /><br />We don't do things slowly, and we don't do bureaucracy. We back high-performance builders who want ownership, early responsibility and the chance to do the most career-defining work of their lives. You'll get the space to try things, the tools to move fast, and the room to see your ideas reach millions of drivers.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do not take our word for it. Read what Zegons say about us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Overview/Working-at-Zego-Insurance-EI_IE1851459.11,25.htm"><u>Glassdoor</u></a>.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to build the future of insurance,<strong> we're hiring.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Purpose of the role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zego’s Complex Claims team is expanding, and we’re on the hunt for a highly skilled Large Loss Claims Handler to join our team. Our large loss specialists handle Zego’s most complex and high value motor claims including those involving brain and spinal trauma, psychiatric injury, complex fractures and pain conditions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this pivotal role, reporting to the Motor Major Loss Manager, you’ll manage your own portfolio of motor cases, focusing on injury claims exceeding £500k. This position requires not only excellent communication and negotiation skills but also a deep understanding of liability, indemnity, and quantum issues to effectively drive down claims costs while ensuring fair compensation for injured claimants.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside handling technical claims, this role involves introducing and executing a quality review programme within the complex loss team, as well as providing mentorship, oversight, and professional development through a structured training scheme.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beyond handling claims, the team works closely with other claims colleagues, reinsurers, panel solicitors, carriers, rehab providers and colleagues across underwriting and pricing to deliver fair, commercially sound outcomes. As a small, highly technical team, we offer broad exposure to grow your career 🚀</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What you'll be working on</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing a portfolio of high value motor claims typically valued between £500k through to £5 million, pre and post litigation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate effectively with customers, witnesses, insurers, repairers, solicitors, and medical agencies to expedite claim resolutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a technical expert within the team, offering guidance and support in large loss scenarios</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the Motor Major Loss Manager and our Head of TP &amp; Complex Claims on Claims strategy and processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Motivate and develop more junior team members by sharing your knowledge and expertise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain Reinsurer and carrier relationships through timely and accurate updates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate, negotiate and settle claims</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calculation of accurate reserves and make decisions on Indemnity and Liability claims</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in strategic projects to keep the team at the forefront of industry trends and performance</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What you will need to be successful</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in managing high value motor bodily injury claims with a current handling authority of at least £250k</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of liability, indemnity, causation, reserving, future losses, the Ogden Discount Rate and complex medical issues</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling litigated claims and applying relevant procedures and frameworks including CPR and MIB technical disputes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for a career in Large Loss and a desire to help shape a growing large loss function</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Zego ways of working 🏡</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teams work better with time to collaborate and space to get things done. We call it Zego Hybrid: some of us are in our office (central London or Halifax) weekly, others monthly or quarterly. It's about finding the balance between face time and focus that produces great work and a healthy life around it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We also make a point of getting everyone in the same room. Teams come together every quarter, and once a year the whole company does, properly. It's a serious investment and consistently one of the best parts of the year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QKOYDx6AMxQ"><u>Here is what the last one looked like</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits 🎁</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Market-competitive salary, benchmarked against your function and reviewed every year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏆 Annual performance bonus, linked to company performance and your contribution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Share options, a real stake in the company and a share in the future you build</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private medical insurance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏖️ Pension, generous holiday, and £1,000 a year to spend on getting to the office or learning something new.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💻 Cutting-edge systems and tools, so you always have what you need to drive your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? We want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zego, leading the AI evolution in insurance.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal opportunities 🌈</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We're an equal opportunity employer and we value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability status.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zego/large-loss-claims-handler-halifax-uk-163248","tags":["Customer Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Halifax","created_at":1792820425},{"slug":"senior-staff-sre-london-227177","company_name":"Uforce","title":"Senior/Staff SRE","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE exists to make aggression unaffordable.<br /><br />Founded in Ukraine and headquartered in London, UFORCE is a defence-technology company with operations across Europe, the United States and Asia.<br /><br />UFORCE builds uncrewed vessels, ground robotics and aircraft, autonomy software, and the command-and-control layer that operates them together. Each platform is deployable on its own, and stronger as part of the system. Its product lines include the MAGURA family of uncrewed surface vessels, the NEMESIS family of strike platforms, the LIUT family of ground robotic platforms, and counter-UAS systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>About the role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">UFORCE is looking for a Senior Site Reliability Engineer to help build and operate the cloud infrastructure platform behind our sovereign mission operations teams. You’ll make it safer and easier to deploy, upgrade, and run UFORCE services in on-premises environments, including sites with limited or no internet connectivity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll combine hands-on infrastructure engineering with practical operational ownership: automating deployments, strengthening reliability, and making sure customer IT and partner operations teams can run the platform with confidence. You’ll work closely with Platform Engineering, Security, and customer-facing teams, with a focus on solutions that are secure, supportable, and usable in the field.</p><h3>What you’ll do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve deployment and maintenance automation for on-premises environments, including infrastructure as code, packaging, environment validation, and preflight checks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make releases and upgrades work reliably in offline or restricted-network settings: manage artifacts and versioning, define validation gates, and document staged rollout and rollback procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop repeatable deployment patterns for VM-based, Kubernetes-based, and mixed environments, and document when and how to handle deviations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish and maintain an observability baseline for constrained environments, including useful metrics, logs, alerts, and dashboards. Make alerts actionable and link them to clear runbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and operationalize service-level objectives and change-safety practices such as smoke tests, rollout checks, and rollback-first procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Respond to incidents across deployed environments, coordinate diagnosis and communication, and turn lessons learned into improvements to automation, monitoring, and operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and maintain operational playbooks, troubleshooting guides, escalation paths, and maintenance workflows for customer IT and partner operations teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with engineering and security teams to identify operational risks early and ensure new platform capabilities are ready to deploy and support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach teammates on practical reliability habits, including debugging, alert quality, incident follow-through, and documentation.</p></li></ul><h3>Required Skills</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant hands-on experience operating production infrastructure or services in SRE, platform engineering, or infrastructure engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and maintaining infrastructure as code with Terraform or a comparable tool, including safe practices for testing and applying changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience with Kubernetes, virtual-machine platforms, or both; an understanding of deployment and upgrade challenges in constrained environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing or operating observability systems for metrics, logs, alerts, and dashboards, including environments that cannot rely on SaaS services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to design safe release, upgrade, and rollback workflows and to make them usable through clear operational documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong incident-response skills: you can investigate ambiguous symptoms, prioritize checks, coordinate with stakeholders, and follow through on corrective actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written and verbal communication, especially when explaining technical risks, procedures, and trade-offs to engineering and operations partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A practical, ownership-oriented approach to reliability: you improve the system and close the loop from incident to prevention.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice to have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with air-gapped, on-premises, or strongly segmented enterprise or defense environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting deployments operated by customer IT teams, third-party operations teams, or managed service providers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with enterprise identity integrations such as Active Directory, LDAP, or SSO, as well as secrets management and auditability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience defining service-level objectives and improving reliability through incident reviews and measurable follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with security or compliance constraints and how to balance them with safe, supportable operations.</p></li></ul><h3>What success looks like</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standard environment setup and refresh becomes faster and more repeatable, with a path to completing common footprints in less than a day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Upgrade and rollback procedures are validated, well documented, and executable by partner operations teams with limited SRE support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">New deployments have usable dashboards and actionable alerts quickly, supported by reusable configuration and runbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer and partner operations teams resolve more routine issues independently, while recurring incidents lead to durable engineering improvements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The nature of combat has changed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tomorrow’s battlefield success depends on autonomy, speed, and adaptability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And UFORCE is ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are You?</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/uforce/senior-staff-sre-london-227177","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom - London","created_at":1792820424},{"slug":"operations-automation-associate-london-185747","company_name":"Nous","title":"Operations & Automation Associate","description":"<h2>About Nous</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nous is a household AI agent. It takes over the bills and admin people don't have time for and acts for them: switching energy, buying insurance, cancelling forgotten subscriptions, managing the family calendar. Nearly 250,000 UK households have signed up, and another joins every minute.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We think the real value of AI isn't writing amazing cover letters, it's doing useful things in the real world for real people. That's the hard part, and a brilliant product is only half of it. An energy switch takes weeks, so our agents run on long-running workflows, not a single chat turn. Cancelling a subscription means a browser agent handling the code Apple sends to your phone. Buying insurance meant getting our regulatory principal comfortable with an agent doing it end to end (a UK first), which comes down to knowing exactly when the LLM should hand over to rules because a mistake would cost someone real money.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're about 30 people running one agent across energy, broadband, mobile, insurance, mortgages and subscriptions (with more being added), each with its own suppliers, rules and ways of going wrong. With far more problems than people, a person or small team owns each one end to end, from spotting it in the data or a customer conversation to shipping the fix. And because the agent acts, you find out quickly whether the fix worked.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everyone builds here: a product engineer launched our subscription cancellation product within a couple of months of joining, and a PM rebuilt our WhatsApp agent.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And it's working. We're growing more than 20x year on year, with a market-leading NPS above +80, and we manage well over half a billion pounds of household spending. We've raised more than $30M from Heartcore, Mosaic and a who's who of entrepreneurs who founded Monzo, GoCardless, lastminute.com and Onfido. But the real draw is the team - ask anyone here why they joined and you'll get some version of "to do great work with really smart people".</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The goal is household life that's simpler, cheaper and fairer, and most of that is still to build.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">What Nous does for members can feel simple: helping them understand their bills, save money, and avoid admin. Delivering that reliably at scale is much harder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join the Operations team at the heart of the business, working on the difficult real-world problems that sit between our members, our product, external suppliers and the systems that make Nous work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a traditional customer operations role. You’ll spend time close to our members, understanding their questions, investigating things that have gone wrong and learning in detail how our service works. We think that matters: the best systems are usually built by people who have seen the underlying problems first-hand.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">But we don’t want you simply to get faster at doing manual work. We want you to spot the pattern, understand why the problem exists, and help build a better way of doing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That might mean redesigning a process, building an automation, using AI to remove repetitive work, querying data to understand what is happening, improving an internal tool, or working with Product and Engineering on a more fundamental fix.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to arrive knowing all of the tools we use. We care much more about how quickly you learn them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for someone early in their career who is unusually curious, quick to learn and good at figuring things out. You might already have built automations or small products yourself. You might instead have worked in operations, consulting, product, analytics or another demanding environment and found yourself constantly looking for better ways to do things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Either way, we want someone who gets excited by a problem they don't immediately know how to solve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll have a lot of support from experienced operators, engineers and product people, but also be given a lot of responsibility unusually early in your career. The aim is for you to quickly become someone who can take an undefined operational problem, understand it properly and build a robust solution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a rare chance to learn how a fast-growing technology company actually works from the inside while building the systems that allow it to scale.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re smart, curious, ambitious and unusually high-agency.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need a long list of technical tools on your CV. We care much more about how you think, how quickly you learn and what you do when you encounter something you don't understand.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll probably thrive here if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have roughly 1–3 years of experience in a demanding environment such as a startup, operations, consulting, product, analytics or similar</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn unusually quickly and enjoy tackling problems you haven't seen before</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are technically curious and actively experiment with AI and new tools to make yourself more effective</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have evidence that you like building things, whether that's automations, side projects, spreadsheets, scripts, internal tools, processes or something completely different</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable getting into the detail and tracing a problem until you understand what is really happening</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can take something messy and ambiguous and impose structure on it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are naturally empathetic and enjoy understanding what a customer actually needs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly and directly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are comfortable working directly with customers and frontline problems, and see that as a source of insight</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership rather than waiting to be told exactly what to do</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is ideal for someone early in their career who wants a steep learning curve, real responsibility and the chance to work as part of a team solving difficult problems.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/nous/operations-automation-associate-london-185747","tags":["Operations (MSO)"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Nous HQ","created_at":1792820424},{"slug":"chief-information-security-officer-ciso-bristol-the-crescent-249992","company_name":"Fractile","title":"Chief Information Security Officer (CISO)","description":"<h1><strong>About Fractile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile was founded in 2022 on the bet that, eventually, the world’s most capable AI systems would be limited in their impact by the time taken to produce useful outputs. We bet everything on the logical conclusion: that the only way to truly unlock this latent value, to make speed viable at scale, was to radically re-invent the hardware that we run our frontier AI models on. Ever since, we have been building chips and systems that tackle this problem: how to efficiently generate output at thousands of tokens per second, while handling the complexity and capacity challenges of operating large models at very long contexts.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The workloads that push to the limits of the current frontier are already transformational; it is the technical and economic limits on inference speed that are constraining progress. The defining work of the 21st century will be marked by the engine of inference delivering immense and diffuse chains of intellectual inquiry, in drug discovery, in software engineering, in materials discovery, in any field where progress is driven by deep reasoning and intelligence to resolve complex problems. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fractile is building the next generation of AI computing technology, developing innovative hardware and software solutions designed to transform the performance and efficiency of AI workloads.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're bringing together exceptional talent across semiconductor engineering, software, and AI to solve some of the most ambitious challenges in computing.</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced and highly technical Chief Information Security Officer (CISO) to lead Fractile's information security, corporate IT, and IT infrastructure functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be responsible for developing and executing a comprehensive technology and security strategy, ensuring Fractile's systems, infrastructure, intellectual property, and business operations are secure, reliable, and scalable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a strategic and hands-on leadership role, combining cybersecurity expertise with ownership of IT operations, infrastructure, and service delivery. You will build and lead high-performing teams, establish robust processes and governance, and ensure our technology environment supports Fractile's rapid growth and engineering ambitions.</p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute Fractile's information security, IT, and infrastructure strategy, ensuring alignment with business objectives, operational requirements, and global growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and oversee corporate IT operations, infrastructure, networks, cloud environments, endpoints, and enterprise systems, ensuring high availability, performance, security, and scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead IT service delivery, including employee technology, hardware and software provisioning, IT support, onboarding and offboarding, asset management, and enterprise applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Protect Fractile's proprietary semiconductor designs, intellectual property, source code, research, and confidential business information against internal and external threats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with engineering teams to ensure secure, reliable, and scalable infrastructure supporting semiconductor development, software engineering, and research environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish and maintain cybersecurity governance, risk management frameworks, policies, and controls aligned with recognised industry standards and regulatory requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead cybersecurity incident response, threat detection, vulnerability management, disaster recovery, and business continuity planning across IT and infrastructure environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee IT and security architecture, including identity and access management, network security, endpoint protection, cloud security, access controls, and secure systems integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage technology vendors, infrastructure providers, third-party security risks, IT budgets, procurement, licensing, and supplier relationships to ensure operational efficiency and value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, lead, and develop high-performing IT, infrastructure, and security teams, advising executive leadership on technology risks, investments, priorities, and operational resilience.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant leadership experience across information security, IT operations, and infrastructure, ideally as a CISO, CIO, VP IT &amp; Security, or equivalent within a technology organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience developing and executing IT, infrastructure, and cybersecurity strategies in complex, high-growth environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical expertise across enterprise IT, cloud infrastructure, networking, systems administration, identity management, endpoint management, and cybersecurity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience building, scaling, and managing IT infrastructure and service delivery functions, including enterprise applications, employee IT support, and operational processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience protecting sensitive intellectual property, proprietary technologies, engineering systems, or research and development environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive understanding of cybersecurity risk management, governance, compliance, and frameworks such as ISO 27001, NIST CSF, and SOC 2</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to establish resilient, scalable, and secure infrastructure, including dis