></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Développer votre autonomie et votre esprit analytique à travers des missions à responsabilités</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Travailler dans un environnement international, en interaction directe avec les filiales et les équipes retail ;</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Acquérir une expérience significative dans le secteur du luxe et se familiariser avec les enjeux du secteur</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;">Vous êtes étudiant(e) en école de commerce, master universitaire ou école d'ingénieur, avec une spécialisation en audit / finance / contrôle de gestion ou équivalent</p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Une première expérience en contrôle de gestion et/ou cabinet d'audit est fortement appréciée.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Une bonne maîtrise d'Excel est indispensable ; un intérêt pour les outils de reporting (Power BI, Tagetik) est un plus. </p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Un niveau d'anglais professionnel est nécessaire pour les échanges avec les filiales.</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Rigoureux(se), motivé(e), curieux(se) et doté(e) d’un véritable esprit d’équipe, vous avez envie de rejoindre un environnement dynamique et bienveillant.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u><span style="color:#000000">Stage de 6 mois conventionné par un établissement reconnu par l’Etat uniquement, à pourvoir en janvier 2027. </span></u></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#121317">Nous sommes convaincus que la diversité de nos équipes est une force. Nous étudions toutes les candidatures avec la même attention, sans distinction de genre, de handicap, d'origine, d'âge ou d'orientation.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/ami-paris/stage-assistante-controle-de-gestion-international-h-f-paris-213056","tags":["Contrôle de Gestion"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Paris, Île-de-France, France","created_at":1792821094},{"slug":"software-engineer-web-full-stack-paris-462123","company_name":"Amo","title":"Software Engineer, Web (Full stack)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for someone to join us as an early member of the Web team, to build and own web platforms that turn large amounts of data into products people love to use. Maps and location data sit at the core of what we build, and we’re looking for an engineer who can take a platform from data model to pixel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In the initial months, you’ll work closely with the team, gradually taking ownership of central systems and features. Given our stage, we’re seeking versatile engineers comfortable contributing across the frontend, the backend and the data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value team members who delve deep into their respective domains, aiming to cultivate a team of subject matter experts with a high sense of ownership. This commitment to expertise is an expectation for every team member.<br /><br /></p><h1><strong>As a Web Engineer, your day-to-day will include:</strong><br /></h1><h2><strong>Platform Engineering</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and building robust, scalable web platforms end-to-end in TypeScript: APIs, services, data access layers and the UI on top of them. You’ll make the architectural decisions and set the patterns that others build on.<br /></p><h2><strong>Workflows &amp; Data Pipelines</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architecting durable, long-running workflows and background processes on our workflow orchestration system (Restate). You’ll also build the pipelines that move data between our warehouse, our databases and our products, reliably and at scale.<br /></p><h2><strong>Data Modeling &amp; Visualization</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Modeling large datasets so they can be queried and visualized fast. That includes choosing the right aggregations, pre-computations and storage across Postgres and BigQuery, and turning them into visualizations that are clear, interactive and beautiful. You’ll handle data with privacy in mind from the very first design decision.<br /></p><h2><strong>Maps &amp; Geospatial Data</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bringing geospatial data to life on the web. You’ll render large amounts of location data on interactive maps, and keep them as fast and polished as they are insightful.<br /></p><h2><strong>Roadmap Creation and Ideation</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributing actively to the roadmap: identifying the right tradeoffs and bringing ideas from both a product and an engineering perspective.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Owning your scope</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be responsible for the architecture, performance, monitoring and reliability of everything you ship. We value engineers who take full ownership of their scope, and who proactively address issues before anyone asks.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h1><strong>Your Skills &amp; Experience:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please indicate your years of experience on the application form.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of professional experience building SaaS products or data-heavy platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High proficiency in TypeScript and Node.js, and in modern web frameworks (React, Next.js…).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience with Postgres and data warehouses (BigQuery, Snowflake, or similar).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of data modeling for analytics and for visualizing large volumes of data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A privacy-aware approach to handling sensitive data, such as aggregation and anonymization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working autonomously across frontend and backend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with workflow orchestration and long-running processes (Restate, Temporal, or similar) is a big plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expertise in map rendering and geospatial data visualization (Mapbox GL, MapLibre, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://deck.gl">deck.gl</a>, or similar) is a big plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with WebGL or GPU rendering is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working closely with backend and data teams across a polyglot stack is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of infrastructure (Bazel, GCP, Kubernetes) is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion and experience building great products. We’d love to hear about things you’ve shipped!<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>AI as a multiplier</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is part of how we build every day. We’re looking for engineers with a real grasp of these tools, who use them to multiply their output and not to make up for missing expertise. You should be able to drive an agent through a complex change, judge what it produces, spot where it’s subtly wrong, and stand behind every line that ships.<br /><br /></p><h1><strong>The bar</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for exceptional engineers, and we set the bar high on purpose. In return, you’ll get real ownership from day one, products used by millions of people, a team that ships in days rather than quarters, a modern stack with top-tier tooling, and colleagues who will push you to grow.<br /><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need to speak French to apply (and you don’t need perfect English; we’ll help you ramp up quickly).<