e full ownership of what they build.<br /><strong>Our values </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Care<br /></strong>We care deeply about our customers, our teammates, and the quality and reliability of what we ship.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bias for Action<br /></strong>We move fast, test in the real world, and iterate quickly rather than over-optimizing in theory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership<br /></strong>We take responsibility end to end, from identifying problems to delivering outcomes and learning from results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As one of Prelude’s first Enterprise Account Executives, you’ll be building the foundations of our enterprise motion, focused on international accounts. You won’t just close deals: you’ll help shape how we sell to the world’s largest companies. You’ll own complex, high-value sales cycles end-to-end, from opening your first enterprise conversations to navigating multi-stakeholder deals and closing top-tier customers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work directly with the founders, partnering closely with product, marketing, and engineering to shape our enterprise motion, refine our messaging, and influence the roadmap based on what customers actually need. Your impact will be visible, measurable, and felt across the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is built for an experienced enterprise AE who wants real ownership: bigger strategic accounts, more autonomy, and a direct hand in building Prelude’s enterprise motion. If you’re excited by fast growth, high standards, and the chance to help build an enterprise sales engine from the inside, this is your seat at the table.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What will you be doing?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning and managing your pipeline across the entire enterprise sales cycle</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identifying and prioritizing high value prospects in our target market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running tailored discovery calls and product demos aligning with prospect pain points</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with Engineering and Product to deliver customized proposals where needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multi-threading across executive, technical and procurement stakeholders to drive deals to close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building and executing strategic plans for your key accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tracking activities and pipeline in our CRM, HubSpot</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharing market feedback to tailor product development and positioning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Iterating and improving sales collateral and pricing models - you’re early enough to help us define “how sales works” at Prelude</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Representing Prelude at key events, conferences, and client meetings</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What are we looking for?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of closing experience in B2B SaaS, including 3+ years managing enterprise accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of exceeding quota and closing new business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence managing a complex full sales cycle, from outbound prospecting through to contract negotiation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling technical products to senior engineering and product leaders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience navigating large organizations: mapping business units and expanding from a first use case across the account</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity and sharp discovery s