dups, now practically AI demo sessions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We see AI not as a replacement for creativity or empathy, but as a multiplier, helping us move faster, think deeper, and serve customers better.<br /><br /><strong>AI use in Recruiting at Gorgias</strong><br />By submitting your application, you agree that Gorgias may collect and process your personal data for recruiting, workforce planning, and related purposes. For more information about how we process your data and your rights, please refer to our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.gorgias.com/legal/applicant-privacy-policy">Applicant Privacy Policy</a>.<br /><br /><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion at Gorgias</strong><br />We’re committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone can thrive. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives because diverse teams drive innovation and better decision-making.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you need accommodations during the application or interview process, please contact us at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- €69,128 – €76,405 • 0.001% – 0.004%</p><ul><li> • €69,128 – €76,405 • 0.001% – 0.004%</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/gorgias/gtm-engineer-growth-paris-22627","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792820426},{"slug":"communications-brand-events-lead-villejuif-53086","company_name":"Orakl Oncology","title":"Communications, Brand & Events Lead","description":"<h1><strong>About Orakl Oncology</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every cancer patient deserves a treatment that works for them. Today, too many never get one in time: fewer than 5% of new cancer drugs make it through clinical trials, and every failure costs patients precious time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orakl exists to change those odds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We bridge biological and artificial intelligence by building large cohorts of virtual cancer patients, combining real patients' tumors with their medical histories and deep biological data. By integrating patient-derived tumor models, experimental biology and AI, we help pharmaceutical companies predict how cancer drugs will perform in patients, identify promising treatments and make better decisions earlier in drug development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2023 by Fanny Jaulin, PhD, Diane-Laure Pagès, PhD, and Gustave Ronteix, PhD, Orakl is a spin-out of Gustave Roussy, one of Europe's leading cancer centres, building on a decade of research. Backed by international investors, we are scaling our technology and partnerships with pharmaceutical companies worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discover more at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://orakl-oncology.com">orakl-oncology.com</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for our first <strong>Communications, Brand &amp; Events Lead</strong> to build Orakl's external presence from the ground up and establish the company as a leading voice in AI-driven cancer drug development. Your job is to make the world understand what we are building, why it matters and why Orakl is uniquely positioned to lead this transformation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will shape how Orakl is perceived by the pharmaceutical companies we partner with, the scientists we want to attract, the investors backing us and the broader industry. From defining our corporate narrative and building our reputation to securing media coverage and putting Orakl in the right rooms, you will turn our scientific and commercial progress into visibility, credibility and meaningful relationships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own our communications, brand and events strategy, working directly with the founders and closely with our scientific, BD and Product Marketing teams. While Product Marketing focuses on our offerings and their commercial value, you will own Orakl's corporate voice, reputation and external presence. You will also lead internal events and support on internal brand alignment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a strategic but highly hands-on role. You will set the direction, build the function and execute much of it yourself, with the autonomy to experiment, make decisions and shape how Orakl grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will need to combine the speed and creativity of a startup with the standards of the pharmaceutical industry. Our communications must be distinctive and ambitious, but always grounded in scientific rigour, evidence and credibility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><h3><strong>Communications and brand: building Orakl's voice</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communications strategy.</strong> Define and execute Orakl's communications strategy across audiences, channels and markets, setting clear priorities that support the company's commercial, scientific, talent and fundraising ambitions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Corporate positioning and narrative.</strong> Own Orakl's corporate story, key messages and tone of voice. Build a distinctive narrative around virtual patients and Orakl's role in advancing cancer drug development, ensuring consistency across the company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Brand identity and presence.</strong> Own and evolve Orakl's brand identity and visual expression across the website, corporate materials, presentations and digital channels, working with designers and external partners when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Content and editorial strategy.</strong> Build and manage an editorial calendar that turns Orakl's scientific breakthroughs, company milestones and industry perspectives into compelling content for the right audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founders' voice and thought leadership.</strong> Build the public profiles of Orakl's founders through LinkedIn, articles, op-eds, interviews and relevant scientific and industry channels. Identify the topics and conversations where Orakl can bring a distinctive perspective.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Press and media relations.</strong> Develop relationships with scientific, pharmaceutical, technology and business media. Identify newsworthy stories, pitch proactively and lead communications around funding, partnerships, scientific advances and company milestones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speaking opportunities.</strong> Build and pitch a targeted pipeline of speaking engagements, panels, podcasts and interviews that position Orakl's founders and scientific leaders as recognised voices in the industry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reputation and scientific credibility.</strong> Ensure all external communications are accurate, evidence-based and consistent with Orakl's scientific standards. Help manage sensitive announcements, complex topics and reputational issues in close collaboration with leadership and scientific teams.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Events: putting Orakl in the right room</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Events strategy and prioritization.</strong> Build Orakl's annual events strategy and calendar, identifying the conferences, industry gatherings and scientific forums that matter most to the business (e.g. JPM, BIO, AACR, BIO-Europe). Define objectives, budgets and expected outcomes for each.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Conference presence and execution.</strong> Own Orakl's participation in major industry events, from sponsorships, booths and speaking opportunities to registrations, logistics, travel, vendors and on-site execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Business development activation.</strong> Work closely with BD and the founders to identify priority contacts, secure relevant meetings and build targeted engagement programmes around key events. Ensure opportunities are captured and followed up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Orakl-hosted events.</strong> Create and run Orakl's own event formats, from intimate scientific dinners and executive roundtables to webinars and partner gatherings, designed to strengthen relationships and generate meaningful conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Event content and experience.</strong> Own invitations, event branding, booth design, signage and communications before, during and after events, working with Product Marketing on offering-specific and scientific commercial content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Event performance.</strong> Evaluate the impact of Orakl's events against their objectives, including strategic relationships developed, meetings secured, commercial opportunities generated and visibility achieved. Use these insights to refine future investments.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Internal communications and culture</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Internal events.</strong> Plan and deliver company off-sites, all-hands gatherings and team celebrations that bring people together and strengthen Orakl's culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Internal brand alignment.</strong> Help teams understand and consistently communicate Orakl's mission, narrative and positioning, ensuring a coherent company voice as the organisation grows.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Building the function</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Processes and partners.</strong> Establish the tools, workflows and external partner network needed to deliver high-quality communications and events efficiently, managing agencies, freelancers and budgets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement and priorities.</strong> Define how communications and events success is measured, focusing on quality of visibility, audience relevance, reputation, strategic relationships and contribution to company objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional collaboration.</strong> Work closely with founders, BD, scientific teams and Product Marketing to identify the strongest stories, align priorities and ensure communications supports Orakl's broader ambitions.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience</strong> in communications, PR, brand or a related role, ideally within life sciences, biotech, healthtech or B2B technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong strategic communications skills</strong>, with experience developing corporate narratives, positioning and communications plans that support business objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exceptional writing and storytelling ability</strong>, from short-form social content and executive ghostwriting to press releases, long-form editorial, website copy and event communications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience in media relations and thought leadership</strong>, with a track record of securing relevant earned media, interviews or speaking opportunities and building executive profiles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ability to communicate complex science</strong>, translating technical and scientific concepts into compelling, accurate stories for pharma decision-makers, investors, scientists and broader audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong editorial judgment</strong>, with the ability to recognize what is genuinely newsworthy, identify compelling angles and choose the right audience, channel and moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience in events and conference management</strong>, from strategic planning and budgeting to hands-on execution, ideally with an understanding of how events can support commercial relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A strong eye for brand and design</strong>, with the ability to maintain high creative standards across digital and physical touchpoints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on and entrepreneurial mindset</strong>, equally comfortable setting a strategy, writing a LinkedIn post, pitching a journalist or running an event on-site.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomy, creativity and pragmatism</strong>, with the confidence to work directly with founders, manage multiple priorities and make things happen in a fast-moving startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent in English</strong>, French is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on-site with occasional remote work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to come from a traditional life sciences communications background. We value people who combine strong storytelling instincts, intellectual curiosity, sound judgment and the ability to make complex ideas accessible without compromising their accuracy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What Orakl offers</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build something from the ground up.</strong> Become Orakl's first Communications, Brand &amp; Events Lead, with the opportunity to define the function, shape its priorities and grow a team as the company scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the voice of an emerging category.</strong> Help establish Orakl as a recognised leader in virtual cancer patients and AI-driven drug development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work at the frontier of AI and cancer research.</strong> Bring breakthrough scientific advances to the audiences and organisations that can turn them into real-world impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership and direct access to leadership.</strong> Work closely with our founders and scientific experts, with significant autonomy, creative freedom and room to grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time to recharge.</strong> 25 days of paid holiday, plus approximately 9 additional rest days (RTT) per year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid working.</strong> 1–2 days per week occasional work from home.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Interview Process</strong></h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager Call:</strong> getting to know each other, aligning on expectations context.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Deep Dive:</strong> detailed conversation about your experience and fit for the role, using examples of what you’ve done and how you like to work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case study:</strong> a take-home case to prepare and then to present in-person to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reference Call:</strong> with one or two former colleagues with whom you worked closely, including a direct manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founder Interview:</strong> A final discussion with at least one founder on vision, culture fit, and mutual ambitions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>👉 More about Orakl </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.welcometothejungle.com/fr/companies/orakl-oncology"><strong>here</strong></a><strong> and </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.orakl-oncology.com/"><strong>here</strong></a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/orakl-oncology/communications-brand-events-lead-villejuif-53086","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Villejuif","created_at":1792820426},{"slug":"product-marketing-lead-villejuif-192763","company_name":"Orakl Oncology","title":"Product Marketing Lead","description":"<h1><strong>About Orakl Oncology</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every cancer patient deserves a treatment that works for them. Today, too many never get one in time: fewer than 5% of new cancer drugs make it through clinical trials and every failure costs patients precious time .</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orakl exists to change those odds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We bridge biological and artificial intelligence by building large cohorts of virtual cancer patients: real patients’ tumors, paired with their medical history and deep biological data. By combining patient-derived tumor models, deep biological data and AI, we help pharmaceutical companies predict how cancer drugs will perform in patients, identify promising treatments and make better decisions earlier in development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We were founded in 2023 by Fanny Jaulin,<strong> </strong>PhD, Diane-Laure Pagès, PhD and Gustave Ronteix, PhD as a spin-out from Gustave Roussy, one of Europe's leading cancer centers, building on a decade of research. We are backed by top international VC investors and we are scaling our technology and partnerships with pharmaceutical companies worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discover more here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.orakl-oncology.com/">Orakl's website</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for Orakl's first <strong>Product Marketing Lead</strong> to shape how we bring our technology to market, from understanding our customers and positioning our offerings to building the commercial narratives and tools that help us win.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will sit at the intersection of science, product and business development, turning complex scientific capabilities into compelling propositions for pharma and biotech customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your job is to understand what our customers need, articulate why Orakl is uniquely positioned to deliver it, and help translate our technology into offerings that customers understand, trust and buy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working directly with our founders, BD and scientific teams, you will own product positioning, go-to-market strategy and commercial enablement, collaborating with our Communications &amp; Events Lead on external launches and campaigns.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role with significant strategic ownership and the opportunity to build Orakl's product marketing function from the ground up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Market intelligence and customer understanding</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer discovery.</strong> Develop a deep understanding of pharma and biotech customers through interviews, prospect conversations and close collaboration with BD. Identify their priorities, decision-making processes, objections and unmet needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer segmentation.</strong> Define and refine Orakl's ideal customer profiles, priority market segments and key buying personas across translational research, clinical development, R&amp;D leadership and BD/licensing teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive intelligence.</strong> Map the competitive landscape, including in-house models, CROs and other AI platforms. Identify where Orakl wins, why it wins and how to communicate its differentiation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market feedback.</strong> Build a continuous feedback loop between customers, BD and scientific teams, translating market insights into recommendations for offering development and commercial strategy.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Product positioning and go-to-market strategy</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offering strategy and positioning.</strong> Work with BD, scientific teams and leadership to translate Orakl's capabilities into compelling commercial offerings, defining target customers, use cases, differentiation and competitive alternatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Messaging and value propositions.</strong> Develop clear, differentiated messaging for each offering and buyer persona, translating complex science into tangible scientific and business value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go-to-market strategy.</strong> Develop go-to-market plans for priority offerings and customer segments, defining target audiences, core propositions, competitive differentiation and commercial activation alongside BD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product launches.</strong> Lead the product marketing side of new offering launches, from positioning and messaging to materials and BD readiness, working with the Communications &amp; Events Lead, who owns external announcements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pricing and packaging.</strong> Support BD and leadership in defining how offerings are structured, packaged and priced based on customer needs, market insights and competitive positioning.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Commercial enablement and impact</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>BD enablement.</strong> Build and own Orakl's commercial toolkit, including pitch decks, one-pagers, case studies, scientific summaries, proposal templates and competitive battlecards, tailored to different customers and use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scientific proof.</strong> Build and maintain a library of validation data, publications, case studies and partner references, translating scientific evidence into credible commercial arguments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team enablement.</strong> Equip BD and scientific teams with the messaging, materials and competitive knowledge they need to communicate Orakl's value consistently and effectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Conference and event content.</strong> Develop product messaging, scientific content and demos for conferences, webinars and industry events, working alongside the Communications &amp; Events Lead, who manages event execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial impact.</strong> Work with BD to understand what drives deal progression, wins and losses. Measure the effectiveness of positioning, messaging and go-to-market initiatives, using customer feedback and commercial data to continuously improve performance.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we are looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5+ years of experience</strong> in product marketing, solutions marketing or a commercially oriented role (such as business development, field applications or consulting) within life sciences, biotech, pharma or scientific technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong scientific foundations</strong>, ideally an MSc or PhD in life sciences or a related field, with the ability to engage credibly with scientists on oncology, translational research and clinical development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Understanding of pharmaceutical R&amp;D</strong>, including how pharma and biotech organisations evaluate, adopt and purchase external technologies and services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic marketing skills</strong>, with experience developing positioning, value propositions, customer segmentation or go-to-market strategies for complex technical products or services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exceptional communication skills</strong>, with the ability to turn sophisticated science into clear, persuasive narratives, presentations and commercial materials.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical and customer-focused mindset</strong>, comfortable conducting market research, analysing competitors and translating customer insights into actionable recommendations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on and entrepreneurial approach</strong>, equally comfortable defining a strategy and executing it, from building a deck to supporting a customer conversation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Autonomy and collaborative instincts</strong>, with the confidence to work directly with founders, scientists and commercial leadership in a fast-moving startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent in English and French</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on-site (our offices in Ile-de-France) with occasional remote work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to have followed a traditional product marketing career path. We value people who combine scientific credibility, commercial judgment and the ability to make complex ideas clear.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What Orakl offers</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build something from the ground up.</strong> Become Orakl's first Product Marketer, with the opportunity to define the function and directly influence our commercial strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work at the frontier of AI and cancer research.</strong> Help bring breakthrough scientific capabilities to the pharmaceutical industry, with the potential to change how cancer drugs are developed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership and direct access to leadership.</strong> Work closely with our founders, scientific experts and commercial team, with significant autonomy and room to grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time to recharge.</strong> 25 days of paid holiday, plus approximately 9 additional rest days (RTT) per year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid working.</strong> 1–2 days per week occasional work from home.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Interview Process</strong></h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager Call:</strong> getting to know each other, aligning on expectations context.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Deep Dive:</strong> detailed conversation about your experience and fit for the role, using examples of what you’ve done and how you like to work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case study:</strong> a take-home case to prepare and then to present in-person to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reference Call:</strong> with one or two former colleagues with whom you worked closely, including a direct manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founder Interview:</strong> A final discussion with at least one founder on vision, culture fit, and mutual ambitions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>👉 More about Orakl </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.welcometothejungle.com/fr/companies/orakl-oncology"><strong>here</strong></a><strong> and </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofo