harma and biotech. You will find the right accounts, reach the right people inside them and turn first conversations into qualified opportunities for the VP Business Development. You will own the front end of Orakl’s commercial engine: account strategy, prospecting, discovery and pipeline discipline. You will work closely with the VP BD, the Product Marketer, the scientific teams and the founders, and alongside the Communications &amp; Events Lead on conferences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Prospects: target, position, engage</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Define where Orakl plays.</strong> Identify and prioritise the pharma and biotech accounts where Orakl’s offerings create the most value, based on their oncology pipelines and development stage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Position Orakl’s offer.</strong> Tailor Orakl’s value proposition to each account’s programmes, priorities and decision makers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Open new relationships.</strong> Engage decision makers at target accounts through direct outreach and introductions from Orakl’s scientific, clinical and investor network.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualify and convert opportunities.</strong> Assess every lead, inbound or outbound, and lead discovery meetings with VPs to understand their programmes, needs, decision process, budget and timing. Hand qualified opportunities to the VP BD.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>BD team: building the structure</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make the pipeline a management tool.</strong> Keep pipeline data reliable so the team and leadership can forecast and decide from it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure what works.</strong> Track conversion by channel and by stage, and focus effort where it delivers results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Market intelligence</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Monitor the competition.</strong> Follow competitors, partnerships and deals in AI and patient-derived oncology models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Inform strategy.</strong> Share market insights with internal teams and leadership to sharpen Orakl’s positioning and priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What we are looking for</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5 to 8 years in business development, sales or account management, selling platforms, data or services to pharma and biotech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of building pipeline from scratch and converting first meetings into qualified opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scientific background (MSc or PhD in life sciences or a related field); comfortable discussing oncology, translational research and clinical development with scientists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A network in pharma oncology or translational teams in Europe or the US is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear writer and confident presenter, at ease with senior scientists and executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on and autonomous in a fast-moving startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English; French a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on-site (our offices in Ile-de-France) with occasional remote work, and regular travel to conferences and clients in Europe and the US.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A central role in building Orakl’s commercial engine, with the opportunity to grow with the BD team as Orakl scales</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct exposure to pharma decision makers and to Orakl’s founders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a fast pacing start up growing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Occasional remote work</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Interview Process</strong></h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager Call:</strong> getting to know each other, aligning on expectations context.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Deep Dive:</strong> detailed conversation about your experience and fit for the role, using examples of what you’ve done and how you like to work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Case study:</strong> a take-home case to prepare and then to present in-person to the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reference Call:</strong> with one or two former colleagues with whom you worked closely, including a direct manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founder Interview:</strong> A final discussion with at least one founder on vision, culture fit, and mutual ambitions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ol><h2><strong>👉 More about Orakl </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.welcometothejungle.com/fr/companies/orakl-oncology"><strong>here</strong></a><strong> and </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.orakl-oncology.com/"><strong>here</strong></a></h2><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/orakl-oncology/senior-business-development-manager-villejuif-223610","tags":["Business"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Villejuif","created_at":1792820426},{"slug":"senior-full-stack-engineer-paris-164464","company_name":"Upflow","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Updated in October 2026</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Target start date:   March 1, 2027</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation:   70,000 to 85,000 EUR yearly gross, depending on profile</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:   Either in-office in Paris (Grands Boulevards, 75002) or full remote on Paris timezone</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About Upflow</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Upflow is the Financial Relationship Management (FRM) platform that helps B2B finance teams collect smarter and get paid by their customers faster, with AI agents working alongside the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, the order-to-cash process is mission critical for businesses, yet it remains fragmented across tools, teams, and workflows. Upflow brings this entire process into one system — four products covering the cycle from invoice to cash (Insights, Collections, Payments, and Cash Application), with AI agents that work alongside the team and a shared intelligence layer underneath.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We serve 500+ companies across 30+ countries, including Vercel, Lattice, and Productboard, and are backed by leading investors including Y Combinator, Hedosophia, Hexa, and Lorimer. With teams across the US and Europe, we're building a category-defining company at the intersection of finance, payments, and AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To learn more about what we do, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://upflow.io">upflow.io</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For a behind-the-scenes look at how we work as a team, head to the Inside Upflow section of our blog at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://upflow.io/blog/inside-upflow">upflow.io/blog/inside-upflow</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join a small, efficient team who builds high-impact features for our users. You'll work on a wide range of topics, including AI agents, workflow automations, analytics, or payment processing. We invest significantly in AI features, and you'll play a key role in making Upflow the leading agentic software in our field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work at a fast pace, averaging 20 deploys to production each day, but with high quality standards, and we value pragmatism, ownership, and a growth mindset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is also transforming how we work, and we're looking for someone eager to use and optimize agents to help us work more efficiently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can be based in our Paris office or work remotely.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your day-to-day, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architect and implement complex, high-impact product features from start-to-finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with the product manager, the designer, and other engineers to translate business requirements into technical solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship clean, maintainable code to production daily.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate actively in technical reviews providing and receiving constructive feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot and debug complex product issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimize application performance and ensure scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help improve our agentic tools and automations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our current stack</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Frontend:</em> Typescript, React, GraphQL</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Backend:</em> Typescript, Node.js, Express, Postgres, and Redis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Infra:</em> GCP, Terraform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Observability:</em> Datadog and Sentry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Github, Copilot, Claude Code, CircleCI</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 5+ years of experience in software engineering.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong proficiency in Typescript, React and SQL.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re proficient at working with agentic coding assistant such as Claude Code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong skills in architecture, software reliability, and scalability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a product sensibility and care about UX.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have good teamwork skills and enjoy providing and receiving feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to work in a startup environment that values excellence, autonomy, and ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in English with strong communication skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are based in Paris, or live in Paris timezone</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why join us</strong></h2><h2></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>International mindset</strong>: We have offices in Paris and New York.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>On-site or full remote</strong>: On-site job in Paris (2-3 days in office), or full remote position on Paris timezone (1 monthly visit in our Paris office).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Exciting moment</strong>: Opportunity to contribute to the Engineering function in the AI era.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>All-star team</strong>: Extremely solid team with deep functional and domain expertise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning opportunity</strong>: Strong focus on learning and growing through education and professional development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trusting environment</strong>: Hands-off management style. We have a strong culture of ownership and autonomy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Best in class perks</strong>: 35 paid days off, meal vouchers, cool offices, top-of-the-range equipment, great healthcare, and competitive salary and equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offsites</strong>: Regular offsites with the team, meetups, and strong connections to the startup ecosystem.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Recruitment Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1 - Screening call</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a discussion with your future manager. We’ll get deeper into your expertise and know-how. We’ll also give you a clearer view of what your day-to-day in that role is like. It’s a good opportunity to see if you foresee yourself working at Upflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2 - Take home assignment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a coding exercise that can only be completed successfully with the help of AI. In addition to delivering working software that meets the requirements, you’ll be evaluated on your product and architectural decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3 - Technical interview</strong></p><p st