es and platforms we admire, now supporting our drive to create the next ones.</p><p>At Homa, we are building the next billion-player experiences from the ground up and shaping the future of entertainment.</p><p>The opportunity</p><p>As an AI Unity Tools Engineer, you'll build the next generation of QA automation and development tooling for Homa's games. This is a new, high-impact initiative, and you'll own it: from the first question to the tools running in production across our portfolio.</p><p>You’ll work across AI, Unity, QA automation, DevOps, and infrastructure to make testing and build pipelines more reliable, scalable, and cost-efficient for games developed by Homa and its studios. You'll be working on AI-driven QA automation at the edge of what is technically possible, and you'll see the impact directly in the speed, reliability, and cost of how our games are made.<br><br>What you'll do</p><ul><li><strong>Build.</strong> Design and deploy AI-enabled QA automation pipelines across Homa's major Unity games.</li><li><strong>Run.</strong> Maintain and improve our TeamCity build pipelines and infrastructure so game builds stay reliable.</li><li><strong>Scale.</strong> Onboard new games and tools onto the platform without reducing service quality.</li><li><strong>Explore.</strong> Test AI-driven approaches to QA that cut manual testing effort and reduce reliance on costly legacy tooling.</li><li><strong>Drive adoption.</strong> Work with developers, QA teams, studios, and mobile teams so the tools you build are actually used.</li><li><strong>Measure.</strong> Track the impact of your work on testing time, build reliability, and cost, and turn it into clear recommendations.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ownership.</strong> You drive outcomes. When a build breaks or a test fails, you fix it instead of explaining why it broke.</li><li><strong>Proactive.</strong> You don't wait for instructions or perfect conditions. You spot what needs doing and do it.</li><li><strong>Pragmatism and simplicity.</strong> You look for the simplest solution that works, use whatever tools are available, and ship. You turn ambitious ideas into practical, achievable solutions.</li><li><strong>Sharp thinking.</strong> You learn fast, reason from facts, and structure your ideas clearly. You can explain a complex technical solution to developers, QA teams, and studios in a few sentences.</li><li><strong>AI-driven.</strong> AI is already part of how you work every day. You've used it to automate, speed up, or rethink at least one thing you're proud of.</li><li><strong>Hungry and motivated.</strong> You're ambitious, high-energy, and grounded. You see this role as a chance to build something new and grow faster than anywhere else, and you're ready to work for it.</li><li><strong>Bonus: you've built something.</strong> An internal tool, a testing framework, a game, a side project. We'd love to hear about it.</li></ul><h3>For this role, you'll also bring</h3><ul><li>Hands-on experience with Unity and the ability to understand Unity games, game systems, and testing contexts.</li><li>Proven experience using AI systems, models, or AI-enabled engineering workflows in practice.</li><li>Strong DevOps understanding, including TeamCity, build pipelines, and infrastructure.</li><li>The ability to work across technical topics while understanding the wider product and business context.</li><li>Experience working in a complex environment with meaningful product and testing volumes.</li></ul><p>Bonus points if you have:</p><ul><li>Experience building QA automation or testing frameworks.</li><li>Experience with AI-driven exploratory testing.</li><li>Experience in gaming or another Unity-based product environment.</li><li>Experience supporting products with high testing volumes.</li><li>Experience driving adoption of internal tools across multiple teams.</li></ul><p>Even if you don't check every box, we encourage you to apply. We value diverse perspectives and backgrounds, and we're more interested in your potential and passion than a perfect match to our checklist.</p><p></p><h3>Why Homa</h3><ul><li><strong>Exceptional growth.</strong> We hire people of outstanding potential, then put them where they can grow fastest.</li><li><strong>Real ownership, early.</strong> This is a new initiative. Your tools will change how Homa and its studios build and test games, and you'll see the results.</li><li><strong>A high talent bar.</strong> Our teams are small and demanding, and the people around you will push you to grow.</li><li><strong>AI at the core.</strong> You'll have access to the best AI tools, and you'll help shape how an AI-first company works.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p>Building great games starts with building a great place to work. Here's what you can expect:</p><ul><li>🏥 Comprehensive Benefits: Depending on your location, you'll enjoy a range of perks such as insurance, meal vouchers, public transport, gym memberships, and more.</li><li>🏢 Paris HQ Access: Enjoy a desk at our private office in a well-located WeWork building that will give you access to WeWork perks like rooftop view and designed coworking spaces.</li><li>🌍 Coworking Access: You will have access to WeWork spaces throughout Europe, along with all their perks and professional office environments.</li><li>🌐 Global Team: Collaborate in English with top-tier talent from 35+ countries, spanning Europe, the UK, the US, and more. Diversity fuels our creativity and innovation.</li><li>✈️ Team Gatherings: We value time together beyond the screen. Join us for occasional team gatherings, off-site retreats (Workations as we name them) to connect, recharge, and celebrate.</li><li>📈 Performance Reviews: We're committed to your growth. Every six months, we reflect on your progress, recognize your achievements, and align on clear development goals.</li><li>💻 Equipment Support: From day one, we'll provide everything you need to do your best work, including a home office setup allowance if you're working remotely.</li></ul><p>Where We Hire</p><p>Our HQ in Paris is a vibrant hub of creativity, collaboration, and connection. From rooftop lunches and coffee chats to after-work apéros and community events, we've designed a space people genuinely enjoy - all within a cosy WeWork filled with good energy (and snacks).</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/homa-games/ai-unity-tools-engineer-paris-367793","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full time","associate"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1792794011},{"slug":"senior-optical-systems-engineer-massy-381593","company_name":"Quandela","title":"Senior Optical Systems Engineer","description":"<h3><em><strong>About Quandela:</strong></em></h3><p>Quandela is a global leader in quantum computing, designing, building, and delivering cutting-edge quantum solutions for research and industry. Its offerings include the most energy-efficient quantum computers for data centers, full-stack quantum computing solutions accessible via the cloud, and algorithm access services for academic and industrial customers. Following a pragmatic, step-by-step roadmap, Quandela has been deploying industrial-grade systems since 2023 while developing future generations of fault-tolerant quantum computers capable of scaling through the integration of thousands of photonic components. Quandela is committed to making quantum computing accessible to all in order to address the most complex industrial and societal challenges. <br>Learn more at: <a href="http://www.quandela.com/" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external">Quandela | Leading Photonic Quantum Computing Solutions</a> </p><p></p><p><em><strong>About this position:&nbsp;</strong></em></p><p>You will join the <strong>QPU Prototyping team</strong>, which develops and integrates the optical systems at the heart of Quandela's quantum processors, turning advanced R&amp;D experiments into operational hardware.&nbsp;</p><p>We are looking for a <strong>Senior Optical Systems Engineer</strong> to take ownership of a major optical development work package within our next-generation QPU programme.&nbsp;</p><p>Your main challenge will be to <strong>maximise optical transmission and system performance</strong>, from experimental characterisation and precision alignment to qualification and integration. You'll tackle complex optical challenges, defining the right experimental approaches and driving solutions from investigation to validation.&nbsp;</p><p>You will also coordinate technical activities involving several engineers and scientists, ensuring the delivery of critical milestones.&nbsp;</p><p>This is a <strong>predominantly hands-on experimental role</strong>, combining deep technical expertise with project ownership.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><p><em><strong>What you'll do:&nbsp;</strong></em></p><p><strong>Develop and optimise optical systems&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Design, assemble, align and operate complex optical setups.&nbsp;</li><li>Characterise optical transmission, identify losses and improve efficiency.&nbsp;</li><li>Define measurement methods and improve stability and reproducibility.&nbsp;</li><li>Troubleshoot experimental challenges and implement reliable solutions.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Qualify and integrate optical subsystems&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Optimise research-developed optical subsystems for QPU integration.&nbsp;</li><li>Define experimental tests, performance targets and qualification procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Collaborate with optics, electronics and system integration teams.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Drive technical delivery&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Own technical deliverables within a major optical development project.&nbsp;</li><li>Coordinate experimental activities across engineers and scientists.&nbsp;</li><li>Plan tasks, milestones, equipment and laboratory resources.&nbsp;</li><li>Anticipate technical risks, resolve blockers and guide contributors.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>The role combines approximately <strong>80% hands-on experimental work and 20% technical coordination</strong>, with no initial requirement for formal people management.&nbsp;<br>-</p><p><em><strong>How you'll grow:&nbsp;</strong></em></p><p><strong>First 3 months:</strong> Become familiar with Quandela's optical systems, experimental infrastructure and qualification objectives.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Within 6 months:</strong> Take ownership of optical characterisation and optimisation activities, coordinating experimental work and technical milestones.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Within 12 months:</strong> Lead the technical delivery of complex optical developments, with increasing autonomy over planning and resources.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Longer term</strong>: Potential progression towards technical team leadership as the team grows.&nbsp;</p><p>-</p><p><em><strong>Requirements&nbsp;</strong></em></p><p><strong>What we're looking for:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>We are looking for an <strong>experienced optical engineer or experimental scientist</strong> with strong hands-on expertise and the ability to drive complex technical projects.&nbsp;</p><p>Relevant backgrounds include<strong> fibered optical systems, laser systems, experimental optics, and optical metrology.</strong> Academic and industrial experience are equally welcome.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Must-have:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>PhD in Optics, Photonics, Physics or related fields.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>&gt;5 years of experimental experience</strong>, including postdoctoral research.&nbsp;</li><li>Hands-on expertise in complex optical systems, alignment and troubleshooting.&nbsp;</li><li>Strong knowledge of linear optics, optical transmission and precision metrology.&nbsp;</li><li>Proven ability to optimise optical performance and solve experimental challenges.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience organising technical work and delivering project milestones.&nbsp;</li><li>Experimental rigour, teamwork and professional English. French is not required.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Important, but you can grow here:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Technical &amp; system integration&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Optical subsystem qualification and hardware integration.&nbsp;</li><li>Python for experimental automation and data analysis.&nbsp;</li><li>Semiconductor optics and quantum optical systems.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Project &amp; operational ownership&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Experimental planning, equipment and resource management.&nbsp;</li><li>Coordination of multidisciplinary technical activities.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Bonus:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Experience transferring R&amp;D setups into operational systems.&nbsp;</li><li>Industrial qualification and reliability standards.&nbsp;</li><li>Experience mentoring engineers or researchers.&nbsp;</li><li>Exposure to quantum computing or advanced photonic hardware.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Quantum computing experience is not required</strong>. What matters is your ability to understand complex optical systems, solve experimental challenges and deliver results.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p><strong>Benefits&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Join a multidisciplinary team developing the optical systems for next-generation quantum processors, with substantial experimental ownership and opportunities for technical progression.&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Competitive compensation aligned with experience.&nbsp;</li><li>Company savings plan and profit-sharing.&nbsp;</li><li>100% health coverage through Alan.&nbsp;</li><li>Transport reimbursement or sustainable mobility bonus.&nbsp;</li><li>Swile meal vouchers.&nbsp;</li><li>Gymlib and childcare support.&nbsp;</li><li>Referral programme.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Process&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Talent Acquisition interview (30–45 min)&nbsp;</li><li>Hiring Manager interview (45–60 min)&nbsp;</li><li>Technical discussion on previous experimental work&nbsp;</li><li>Technical case study or presentation with the team&nbsp;</li><li>Reference checks&nbsp;</li><li>Team meeting&nbsp;</li><li>Offer&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Beyond that:&nbsp;</strong></p><p>At Quandela, we value diverse scientific and engineering backgrounds, practical curiosity and the ability to learn from different fields.&nbsp;</p><p>Whether your experience comes from an academic laboratory, industrial R&amp;D or a different area of experimental optics, we'd love to hear from you if you enjoy tackling demanding technical challenges and turning experimental work into reliable results.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/quandela/senior-optical-systems-engineer-massy-381593","tags":["Computer Hardware"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Massy, France","created_at":1792783214},{"slug":"responsable-commerciale-showroom-management-des-equipes-h-f-arcueil-444106","company_name":"Mia Couture","title":"Responsable Commercial(e) – Showroom & Management des équipes (H/F)","description":"<h2>L'art du sur-mesure au service de nos clientes</h2><p>Mia Couture est une maison de couture parisienne installée à Arcueil, dédiée à la création de robes de mariée et de soirées uniques. Depuis plus de dix ans, notre atelier conjugue savoir-faire artisanal et raffinement pour accompagner chaque future mariée à travers une expérience exclusive, du premier croquis jusqu'aux derniers essayages. Pour structurer notre organisation et accompagner notre croissance, nous cherchons un(e) Responsable Commercial(e) pour piloter l'activité de notre showroom et encadrer l'équipe au quotidien.</p><h2>Vos missions au quotidien</h2><p>Vous prenez la direction opérationnelle du showroom d'Arcueil avec une autonomie complète sur le pilotage de la performance commerciale et l'organisation de la boutique. Vous encadrez l'équipe de conseillères de vente et de créatrices, animez les temps forts de la vie du showroom et garantissez l'excellence de l'expérience client dans le respect des codes du luxe. Vous suivez les indicateurs de vente, optimisez les processus d'accueil et veillez à la concrétisation des projets de nos clientes.</p><h2>Ce que nous attendons de vous</h2><ul><li><p>Expérience confirmée dans le management d'équipe et le pilotage de la performance commerciale, idéalement dans l'univers du retail haut de gamme ou du sur-mesure.</p></li><li><p>Sens aigu du service client, de l'élégance et rigueur dans le suivi des ventes.</p></li><li><p>Capacité à fédérer une équipe autour d'objectifs communs et à organiser le quotidien d'un showroom.</p></li></ul><h2>Votre cadre de travail et avantages</h2><p>Vous disposez d'un ordinateur portable pour vos tâches quotidiennes. Vos frais de transports publics sont partiellement pris en charge. Vous bénéficiez de modules de formation professionnelle pour accompagner votre prise de poste et faire évoluer vos compétences.</p><h2>Rémunération</h2><p>La rémunération proposée pour ce poste s'établit entre EUR 2,700 et 3,600 par mois.</p><h2>Vos premiers mois à Mia Couture</h2><p>Dès vos premières semaines, vous prendrez en main la gestion quotidienne du showroom d'Arcueil et nouerez un contact privilégié avec notre équipe. Vous structurerez le suivi des indicateurs commerciaux et prendrez rapidement vos repères dans l'accompagnement de nos clientes pour garantir la qualité de service propre à la maison.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mia-couture/responsable-commerciale-showroom-management-des-equipes-h-f-arcueil-444106","tags":["Management","Team Leader"],"job_types":["Cdd - contrat à durée déterminée","manager / superviseur"],"location":"Arcueil","created_at":1792780250},{"slug":"software-engineer-fullstack-kotlin-react-paris-paris-235143","company_name":"Doctolib","title":"Software Engineer Fullstack Kotlin / React (x/f/m)","description":"&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a team of passionate and hardworking entrepreneurs to transform healthcare!&lt;/p&gt;
