pré.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je werkt nauwkeurig en gestructureerd. Je krijgt energie van een overzichtelijke en goed bijgewerkte planning tool.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent proactief: je ziet een uitdagingen aankomen voordat ze er zijn en denkt mee over hoe we elke dag efficienter kunnen plannen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent toegankelijk en staat net zo graag in contact met onze medewerkers als achter je scherm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent communicatief sterk in het Nederlands en Engels, zowel mondeling als schriftelijk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent minimaal 32 uur per week beschikbaar en werkt vanuit ons warehouse in Amsterdam, midden tussen de collega’s voor wie je plant. In het weekend sta je af en toe stand-by.</p></li></ul><h1>Wat wij bieden</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Werken bij een B Corp gecertificeerd bedrijf, waarbij je de kans krijgt om je stempel te drukken op het Europese voedselsysteem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een extra vrije dag per jaar om je in te zetten voor vrijwilligerswerk en iets goeds te doen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aandacht voor je mentale gezondheid met online begeleiding van erkende psychologen via OpenUp.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voor straks een perfect pensioen via BPFL.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Elke maand food for thought, met workshops en talks via de Crisp University.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enthousiaste, slimme collega’s en tijd om elkaar te leren kennen tijdens sport, events en proeverijen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">En... fikse korting op je Crisp boodschappen, omdat je thuis natuurlijk ook goed wilt eten.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/crisp/personeelsplanner-amsterdam-335801","tags":["Warehouse"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792820426},{"slug":"business-control-intern-amsterdam-309367","company_name":"Datasnipper","title":"Business Control Intern","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />As our Business Control Intern, you’ll join the Finance team and work closely with the Business Controller. You’ll help leadership understand how the business is doing and where it’s going. As part of your work, you’ll handle monthly reporting on our financial performance and prepare the board deck for the management team. This is a hands-on role with real responsibility, and you’ll also help us rethink how Finance works by automating manual steps with AI. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why DataSnipper?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe trust is essential to how society works. Every day, we rely on information that's been independently verified, from financial statements to the products we buy, to the sustainability claims companies make. Behind that trust are audit and finance professionals who examine evidence, verify information and hold organizations accountable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DataSnipper, we build AI solutions that empower those professionals to make those judgements. With Alwin by DataSnipper, our new agentic platform, AI agents now take on end-to-end audit and finance procedures, while every conclusion stays traceable to its source. That frees professionals to focus on the judgment and expertise that make their work so important.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're trusted by Fortune 500 companies, government agencies and all Big Four audit firms. Today, more than <strong>600,000 professionals across 3,000+ organizations in 175 countries </strong>rely on our platform, and in 2025 alone DataSnipper delivered more than <strong>$1.4 billion</strong> in productivity savings to its customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a $100 million Series B led by Index Ventures, at a $1 billion valuation, we've built a strong foundation for what's next. And as proud members of 1% for the Planet, we care about how we grow, not just how fast.</p><h2><br /><br /><strong>In this role, you will:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor business performance and report on key financial and operational metrics (with a focus on ARR growth)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform variance analysis between forecasts and actuals, and explain what’s driving the gaps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support monthly and quarterly reporting, including the board deck for the management team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help the Business Controller gather inputs for forecasts, making sure the data is accurate and relevant</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the team on projects that drive business growth, profitability and operational excellence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Streamline and automate existing processes using the AI tools available to you</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you are:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a student pursuing a Master’s in Finance or Accounting, with a strong academic track record                                                                               </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable in Excel and enjoy building clean, reliable models and reports                  </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re AI-forward. You already use AI tools to speed up data pulls and reporting, and you’re always looking for the next manual step to automate                     </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re detail-oriented and organized, and you double-check numbers before they reach leadership                                                                                                                                                        </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re curious: you ask “why” behind the numbers and want to learn how a SaaS business works</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We Offer</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internship duration: <strong>6 months </strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being part of one of the fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups in the Netherlands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International and collaborative work environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delicious daily lunch prepared fresh by our chef in the Amsterdam office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fun team events and social activities.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 <strong>If this sounds like you, apply now!</strong> We can’t wait to welcome our next intern.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At DataSnipper, we believe great ideas come from different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. We are committed to building an inclusive workplace and providing every candidate with a fair and equitable hiring experience.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our hiring decisions are merit-based and grounded in the skills, experience, potential, and capabilities relevant to the role.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We welcome applicants regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, disability, or any other characteristic that makes you, you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>What matters to us is what you can bring to the role, the team, and DataSnipper.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/datasnipper/business-control-intern-amsterdam-309367","tags":["Finance & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792820426},{"slug":"quantum-hardware-assembly-technician-delft-200559","company_name":"Quantware","title":"Quantum Hardware Assembly Technician","description":"<h2><strong>About Us </strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">QuantWare is building the world’s most powerful quantum processors to solve humanity's greatest challenges. We do this with our unique VIO™ technology, the only QPU architecture that breaks the hardware barriers that have held quantum computing back, unlocking the path to MegaQubit quantum processors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With VIO, we are paving the way for the hyper-scale quantum computers that will change the world. And delivering on that vision demands people who don’t shy away from tackling the hardest challenges of our time. That’s where you come in! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our <strong>Quantum Hardware Assembly Technician</strong> at QuantWare, you are the hands that turn a quantum chip into a working, measurable product. You package our chips into their housing and onto a PCB, and you will assemble and mount the new devices into their cryo fridge in the test facility. Your precision, discipline and reliability directly keep our production and measurement pipelines moving, and ensure our quantum hardware meets the highest quality standards.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>hands-on execution role</strong>. You carry out chip assembly and fridge loading according to technical drawings and documented work instructions (SOPs), to a consistent quality standard and pace, and you record your work in our production systems. You report to the <strong>Production Manager</strong>, who holds formal line-management responsibility (1:1s, performance reviews, absence and leave). You take your daily and weekly priorities from the <strong>Assembly Tech Lead</strong>, who sets the assembly schedule and is the technical authority on the floor; fridge loading is planned in close coordination with the measurement team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Core Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Assemble quantum chips into their packaging</strong>, working from technical drawings and work instructions to place and mount the chip in its housing and mount the chip in its housing with the PCB.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make the electrical connections</strong>, wirebonding (manual and automatic) will be a significant part of the daily activities, as well as manual soldering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure and test your work</strong>, performing the defined electrical and mechanical checks and recording the results, so issues are caught before a device moves on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finish and close the package</strong>, including sealing, inspection, laser engraving and preparing for transportation to the measurement location.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Load our cryogenic fridges with new chips to be measured</strong>, mounting packaged samples and QPUs, making the wiring, thermal and mechanical connections, and closing up the system with magnetic shields. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Safeguard quality</strong>, handling fragile, high-value parts with care and following handling and ESD procedures, because a single scratch, particle or ESD event can ruin a chip.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supporting Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flag deviations early</strong>, stopping and raising it with the Assembly Tech Lead when something does not match the instruction or does not look right, rather than improvising a fix.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help improve how we work</strong>, giving practical feedback on work instructions, fixtures and tools while our processes are still maturing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep a safe, clean and organised workplace</strong>, applying 5S and HSE rules every day and making sure your bench, tooling and consumables are ready.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MBO-level technical education (level 3 or 4) or equivalent, for example in mechatronics, mechanical engineering, electronics, fine-mechanical or precision engineering, or lab or instrument technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">4+ years of hands-on experience assembling mechanical, electrical or mechatronic systems; relevant internships count.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to read work instructions with photos and technical drawings, and comfortable with basic digital tools and production systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good with your hands at two scales: precision in assembly, handling of fine devices and connectors, and mechanical assembly such as bolting, cabling and fitting larger parts together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Precise and patient, with a genuine liking for detailed hands-on work done well, every time, and a practical approach to solving problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with structured, repeatable work, and disciplined about following instructions step by step and recording what you did.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable in an environment that is still being built, where not every process is finished yet and priorities can shift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A team player in a young, driven team who communicates openly and speaks up when something isn't right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good command of technical English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus if you also bring:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with wirebonding, die attach or other chip-packaging / microelectronics assembly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with measurements, diagnostics or troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a lab, ESD-controlled or 5S production environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience assembling, servicing or setting up complex equipment, instruments or machines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with cryogenics or vacuum systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don't tick every box? Apply anyway! <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://hbr.org/2014/08/why-women-dont-apply-for-jobs-unless-theyre-100-qualified">Research</a> shows women often self-select out if they don't meet every requirement. Here's our take: nobody ticks every box. This is a description of our ideal candidate, not a filter. If most resonates and you're keen to learn the gaps, apply. We hire for trajectory, not perfection. <br /><br /><strong>What We Offer:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At QuantWare, you’ll be part of a high-performing team of world-class experts in an ambitious, fast-moving environment. From day one, you’ll have the trust, tools, and support to do your best work. Here’s what you can expect:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive salary</strong> - A salary that reflects the impact and importance of the role (and of course 8% holiday allowance)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension that’s built to last</strong> - A generous and future-proof pension plan that includes partner and dependent coverage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility built on trust</strong> - We focus on outcomes. Work flexibly, in a hybrid setup, with an open vacation policy that lets you manage your time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth</strong> - We invest in your L&amp;D, with a budget available to each team member, dependent on their individual ambitions, development needs, and performance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A connected team</strong> - We make space to celebrate wins together, with team events, offsites, and spontaneous moments that bring us closer<br /><br /><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion at QuantWare</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an ambitious company, not only for our goals but also to become an even more diverse and inclusive team. We know great candidates don't always follow a straight path, and we value diverse experience, perspectives, and ways of thinking. We know this helps us make better decisions, drives more innovation, and strengthens our culture. <br /><br /><em>As part of our recruitment process, candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening.</em></p><h2></h2><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/quantware/quantum-hardware-assembly-technician-delft-200559","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1792820426},{"slug":"senior-accountant-amsterdam-215724","company_name":"Wetravel","title":"Senior Accountant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, I'm Serhii, I'm the Accounting Team Lead at WeTravel, and I'm hiring the Senior Accountant to take over the work I've done for the past three years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">I joined as a Junior Accountant, took on this scope early, and grew into leading the accounting</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">team. That path is real here: if you own your work and keep improving how it gets done, scope</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">follows. You'll report to me, and I'll be your day-to-day partner, reviewer and someone to think</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">problems through with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a small team, so your work is visible and your ideas get used. We value autonomy: you get clear ownership, not a checklist and someone looking over your shoulder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care about the "how" as much as the "what." We write standard operating procedures (SOPs), build reusable workpapers, script repetitive NetSuite tasks and use AI tools daily to move faster. If you've ever rebuilt a reconciliation so the next month took half the time, you'll fit in. We're remote-first. Our finance team works mostly from home, split between Amsterdam and the US, so you'll collaborate across time zones. You and I will meet at our Amsterdam office for in-person days, such as working sessions, close kick-offs and planning. How often depends on what the work needs, and we keep it flexible. The office is open every day if you'd rather work from there. You'll need to live in the Netherlands, within reach of Amsterdam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our values:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Be Respectful: we build an inclusive team that values different perspectives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Be Honest: we default to transparency, including when something in the numbers is wrong.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Be Resourceful: we find a way forward even when the path isn't mapped out.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Be the Solution: spotting a problem is the start; fixing it is the job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll own</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own these areas end to end, from monthly entries through audit support.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•<strong> Month-end close: </strong>you'll be the main preparer of the monthly close, owning accruals, prepaids</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">and balance sheet reconciliations, and reviewing the income statement for accuracy, correct</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">periods and department mapping before it goes to final review.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Cash: bank, card and payment-platform accounts across multiple currencies and entities,</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">including Stripe, Airwallex, ING and Corpay.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•<strong> Intercompany:</strong> intercompany entries and loan agreements with interest between entities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Leases and fixed assets:</strong> lease accounting (right-of-use assets and liabilities), leasehold</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">improvements, fixed assets, intangibles and depreciation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Compensation: </strong>bonus and commission accruals, payroll journal entries and liabilities, pension</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">and 401(k).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Expenses and AP:</strong> the full expense cycle, from vendor bills and card spend to prepaid</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">amortization, AP tie-outs and department mapping.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•<strong> VAT: </strong>preparing BV VAT returns for review.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Audits:</strong> owning your areas in the annual financial audit and tax reviews.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•<strong> Process: </strong>documenting and improving what you own, from standard operating procedures</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">(SOPs) to automation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• <strong>Reporting: </strong>presenting your areas to the finance team in a weekly review.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care most about how you work, then what you know. Audit firm or in-house, scale-up or</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">corporate: your background matters less than what you've owned.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why You Should or Shouldn't Apply</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You should apply if you have:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• A track record of owning close areas end to end without needing someone to drive them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• 3+ years in accounting, with hands-on month-end close experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Multi-entity and multi-currency experience, including intercompany.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Solid grounding in accrual accounting; US GAAP experience, or the willingness to get there</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">quickly alongside Dutch GAAP.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Strong Excel or Google Sheets skills and experience with a mid-market ERP (NetSuite ideal).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Fluent English, written and spoken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• A bachelor's degree in accounting or finance, or equivalent experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• NetSuite and Ramp experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Dutch VAT or statutory reporting exposure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Examples of processes you've automated or documented, with or without AI tools.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• Interest in growing your scope and responsibilities over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You shouldn't apply if:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• You prefer a role where every process is fully documented and never changes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• You need regular check-ins to keep month-end tasks moving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• You'd rather flag a problem than dig in and propose a fix.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">• You're uncomfortable explaining your numbers, or saying when you got something wrong.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Benefits</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous "Time to Recharge" policy — enjoy unlimited paid time off to rest, recharge, and show up as your best self.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work remotely for a maximum of 4 weeks per calendar year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-week cross-functional onboarding program.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cycle-to-work scheme (Swapfiets subscription) or commuting reimbursement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monday and Thursday lunches and after-work social events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Beautiful office in central Amsterdam – rooftop garden</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive paid family leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Three paid volunteer days per year — take time to give back to causes you care about, on us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cutting-edge equipment and tools to set you up for success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join an international, travel-loving team with a passion for adventure and innovation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employer-sponsored pension plan with a 2% employer contribution deposited into your individual pension account<em>.</em></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to a 10%  group discount on supplementary/additional health insurance (aanvullende verzekeringen), with the same discount available to eligible family members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our Booking Marketplace: Book hotels and flights for personal travel at exclusive discounted rates.</p></li></ul><h2>Equal Opportunities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">WeTravel is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. If you're excited about this opportunity and believe you're a good fit, we encourage you to apply and join us in transforming the travel industry!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €57.4K – €63.8K</p><ul><li> • €57.4K – €63.8K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/wetravel/senior-accountant-amsterdam-215724","tags":["Finance & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792820425},{"slug":"head-of-partnerships-europe-amsterdam-103539","company_name":"Vio","title":"Head of Partnerships (Europe)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.vio.com/">Vio</a>, we believe booking accommodation should feel fair and effortless, never overwhelming or unclear.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As one of the world’s most innovative travel tech platforms, we help millions of users make smarter travel decisions by comparing stays across 100+ booking sites so that they can find the best place, at the best price, anywhere in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our goal is to help travellers book like an insider. That means cutting through the noise and complexity of hotel booking and surfacing real value with clarity, transparency, and full support. No tricks. No confusion. Just great stays, booked with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With operations in 100+ markets and growing fast, our mission is to reshape how people discover and book accommodation through technology that travelers can trust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vio offers a variety of excellent product solutions that compliment travel and non-travel products, and our partner solution program has been a great success since foundation, and in 2026 YTD its growing 300% YoY. You would be joining a rocketship and have the product support to succeed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we’re looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced Business Developer to help us scale our efforts in the European market and forge creative, win-win partnerships with the best companies in the space.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vio is in a position every exceptional sales leader can appreciate: an outstanding product, and a partner solutions team that works hand-in-hand with the product team — making partnerships faster to launch and easier to scale. The challenge? We're still building brand recognition in Europe. Opening doors is the first hurdle; finding the right fit and scaling what works is the next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We need an exceptional business leader who is fluent in travel distribution — someone who instantly understands how metasearch works, how OTAs differ from one another, and which types of API integrations different partners would benefit from. At the same time, this role is largely about selling <em>outside</em> of the travel industry: targeting general-purpose tech and e-commerce companies that have travel reach but no product of their own. That requires both a strong network in the broader tech space and the ability to rapidly build new connections.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive new business by introducing Vio's suite of solutions to tech and e-commerce partners across Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of our existing prospects pipeline and convert prospects into active, long-term partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Uncover new use cases and solutions by listening closely to partner needs, and work cross-functionally to shape what we build next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A travel industry veteran with experience in accommodation marketplaces — either OTAs or metasearch — or flight distribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-starter motivated by commercial success and long-term, mutually beneficial partnerships. You have strong skills across tech, data, and legal that allow you to drive most deals to closure independently.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join us now?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vio is an exceptional innovator in the accommodation booking space, using modern technology and a customer centric approach to innovate in ways few can. Bringing our platform to Millions of new users increases the competitiveness of the travel market and raises the bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In early 2027 we are introducing our bookable API: a modern OTA offering that is built atop of our UX, Product, Supply and customer facing infrastructure and enables partners to build a customised and exceptional experience with little investment, using advances in AI and Vio’s unique market position.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our partner solutions unit has seen great growth in 2026 and is now Vio’s strategy driver. It is an exciting time to join as we mature our offerings and broaden the partnership base.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We reward our employees for the value they create by granting <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viodotcom/why-findhotel-offers-share-appreciation-rights-sar-1b688867d8c4">Stock Appreciation Rights</a> to all employees.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of chances to learn and grow within an open, diverse culture that promotes knowledge sharing, trust, and transparency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A great compensation package, perks, and benefits – including significant stock appreciation rights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible time off, with as many holidays as you need, and a chance to work remotely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be part of an <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viodotcom/2021-our-people-in-numbers-b72145c3fa9b">international team</a> in one of the best office locations in Amsterdam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value good food and offer catered lunches from various cuisines, great coffee, and the occasional barbecue in our garden.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We enjoy getting together to celebrate our wins, with company events in Amsterdam and abroad.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A budget for your home office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to free mental health support via <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://openup.com/">OpenUp</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We encourage people from all ethnic groups, genders, sexualities, ages, and abilities to apply. If this job description resonates with you, we’d love to hear from you.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please note: Although this role can be remote , we prefer candidates based in EMEA zones. The alternative are candidates who know this geographical market extremely well and able to work in these time zones.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📖 Blog posts worth reading</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viotdotcom/our-core-values-and-what-they-mean-to-our-people-2880e69413c1">Our Core Values and What they Mean to our People</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/@viodotcom1/vio-com-reimagining-metasearch-for-travelers-aa41548eebee">Re-Imagining Metasearch for Traveling</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/lifeatviodotcom/">Instagram</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ----- to see what life at Vio looks like.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vio/head-of-partnerships-europe-amsterdam-103539","tags":["Partnerships & Business Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands - Employee","created_at":1792820423},{"slug":"remote-disputes-chargebacks-manager-179624","company_name":"Vio","title":"Disputes & Chargebacks Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Vio.com">Vio </a>we believe booking accommodation should feel smart, fair, and effortless — never overwhelming or unclear.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As one of the world’s fastest-growing travel tech platforms, we help millions of users make smarter travel decisions by comparing stays across 100+ booking sites — so they can find the perfect place, at the best price, anywhere in the world. We cut through the noise and complexity of hotel and vacation rental booking, surfacing real value with clarity, transparency, and full support. No tricks. No confusion. Just great stays — booked with confidence. With operations in 100+ markets and growing fast, our mission is to reshape how people discover and book accommodation through technology travelers can trust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for an experienced <strong>Disputes &amp; Chargebacks Manager</strong> to own and continuously improve our disputes function end to end.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be accountable for two closely connected areas: <strong>dispute management</strong> and <strong>chargeback representment</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">On dispute management, you’ll own how we identify and respond to dispute trends, improve prevention, strengthen evidence, and coordinate effectively with internal teams and external partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">On chargeback representment, you’ll own the operational health and performance of the process including case quality, deadlines, win rates, team effectiveness, partner performance and automation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role requires operational ownership with the goal of improving dispute outcomes while scaling the function efficiently as volumes grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>☑️ What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the dispute operation day to day, making sure cases are handled accurately and on time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage volume, workload and escalations across the team and our outsourced partners, holding partners to clear targets on quality, speed and cost</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review representments and evidence, coach the team, and set the quality bar</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide when to fight, accept or escalate a dispute based on evidence, value and effort</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyse won and lost cases to sharpen strategy, and flag unusual dispute or fraud trends quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Customer Support, Product, Finance, Payments and Fraud to reduce avoidable disputes through changes to fraud rules, refund policies, communication and the product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Redesign workflows around automation, including triage, evidence gathering, deadline tracking and AI-assisted drafting with human review</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Data and Engineering to build reliable reporting on dispute performance</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔎 Who you are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 5+ years of hands-on experience in disputes and chargebacks, including writing representments yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know dispute lifecycles, reason codes, evidence requirements and representment strategy in depth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have led a disputes and chargebacks function, including team performance and operational delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You find trends, risks and opportunities in data, and turn them into concrete process changes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have set quality standards and coached people to meet them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: experience in travel, hospitality or marketplaces where the company is the merchant of record; managing outsourced dispute teams; scaling a manual operation with tooling, AI or automation; and working with card scheme monitoring programmes and chargeback-ratio thresholds</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first months, you’ll work live cases yourself, set a trusted baseline for performance, and launch the first automation initiative. By month six, we expect measurable improvement in win rates, quality and cost, and a working loop with other teams that prevents avoidable disputes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join us now?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are one of the most innovative and fastest-growing accommodation booking platforms in the world today, having grown our bookings 30x between 2017 and 2025, and catering to the needs of over 100 million unique visitors worldwide each year. We do that by harnessing the power of advanced algorithms and an innovative suite of power features and managed to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viodotcom/how-to-survive-refocus-thrive-again-as-a-travel-startup-in-corona-times-c656ef748a10">overcome the corona crisis remarkably fast</a>;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The mobile applications (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/vio-com-book-hotel-deals/id1639101398">iOS</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.vio.mobileapp&amp;hl=en_US&amp;gl=US">Android</a>) we launched in 2023 are already a big success, reaching 5 million installs with great customer reviews, as we are beginning to build <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Vio.com">Vio </a>as the brand for value-seeking travellers worldwide;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a passionate and diverse team of tech enthusiasts and creatives with a commitment and focus on the traveler above all else - and it shows in our industry-leading <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.trustpilot.com/review/vio.com">TrustPilot score</a>;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We place huge importance on rewarding our employees for the value they generate by giving <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viodotcom/why-findhotel-offers-share-appreciation-rights-sar-1b688867d8c4">Stock Appreciation Rights</a> to all employees.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do you want to know if <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Vio.com">Vio</a> is the right place for you? Find out by reading <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viodotcom/who-are-we-looking-for-at-findhotel-cf1ccc1dce8c">about the attitude that thrives at </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Vio.com">Vio. </a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plenty of chances to learn and grow within an open, diverse culture which promotes knowledge sharing, trust and transparency;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A great compensation package, perks and benefits (including significant stock appreciation rights);</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible time off (take as many holidays as you need) and a chance to work remotely;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be part of a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/viodotcom/2021-our-people-in-numbers-b72145c3fa9b">highly international team</a> that enjoys working, eating and playing together in one of the best office locations in Amsterdam;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value good food and offer catered lunches from various cuisines, great coffee, and the occasional barbecue in our garden;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We enjoy getting together to celebrate our wins with company events in Amsterdam and abroad;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A budget for your dream home office;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to free mental health support via <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://openup.com/">OpenUp</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vio/remote-disputes-chargebacks-manager-179624","tags":["Operations & Facilities"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1792820423},{"slug":"software-engineer-java-logistics-amsterdam-48094","company_name":"Teampicnic","title":"Software Engineer (Java) - Logistics","description":"&lt;section class=&quot;section vacancy-detail-intro-section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section-inner&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;entry-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Java teams in the Logistics domain make sure that our products travel all the way from the suppliers in our electronic vehicles, and arrive at our customers’ houses with a smile. From optimizing our routes, to making our drivers’ lives easier, to planning and executing all inbound and outbound products: there’s a wide range of products to work on. Through designing, developing, and testing new features, or improving the scalability and security of our platform: you’ll be owning a product together with your team, while finding yourself fully immersed in an engaging scaleup culture. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tricks of the trade&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;: Take ownership of projects from concept to delivery, aligning technical solutions with business goals with a product engineering mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem solving&lt;/strong&gt;: You see a problem, you tackle it with technology - with your users always in mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;: Design, test, evolve, and evaluate the systems that underpin our Logistics operations, offering a creative and analytical approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech: &lt;/strong&gt;Java 21/25 (Spring 6 with Spring Boot 3.5, Reactor, Immutables, Maven), React, Angular, RabbitMQ, Kafka, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Git, Docker, AWS, Helm, Terraform, Kubernetes, Vault, Datadog, Python 3.x&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a Master’s Degree (in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Information Technology, Computer Engineering or a related technical field) or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a product mindset: you own and solve business problems through tech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 1-5 years of professional experience in programming and software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a profound understanding of software development principles and are ready to have hands on backend and frontend alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your English skills are on point (no Dutch required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re based in or happy to relocate to the Netherlands*&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* We work from our office in Amsterdam. Being present makes a genuine difference to your team and the work. There&#39;s flexibility to work from home when needed, but if remote or hybrid-first is what you&#39;re after, this probably isn&#39;t the right fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please send your CV in English for complete consideration.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Picnic Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;✍🏼 Mastery is a journey!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get plenty of opportunities to challenge yourself and grow, including the Picnic Tech Academy, Lunch &amp;amp; Learn sessions, and tailored soft skills training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💡 Make a difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work on real-world problems, seeing the impact of your work every day in our warehouses and in our satisfied customers. Plus, our fully electric vehicles and sustainable business model mean you’ll also be contributing to making the world a better place!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🫱🏼‍🫲🏾 Teamwork makes the dream work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 80 nationalities across 3 countries, you’ll be part of a diverse company with plenty of cool stuff to get involved with, from board game evenings, to after-work drinks, to our company ski trip and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍎 You are what you eat&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll get freshly prepared, healthy lunches and snacks (with plenty of vegetarian, vegan, and halal options). Coffee snob? Don’t worry, our amazing Picnic barista has you covered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🚴🏽 Stay healthy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mental health is important. As well as having the option to speak with Picnic colleagues who act as confidential advisors, our collaboration with OpenUp gives you easy access to professional psychologists, along with workshops and materials. There are plenty of sports communities and events to get involved with, from tennis to yoga, to climbing!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🔋 Attractive package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer competitive compensation and a pension plan that looks out for your future self, as well as 25 vacation days per year, so you can recharge your batteries&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌍 Benefits for expats&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It can be daunting starting a new job AND moving to a new country. That’s why we offer lots of support for our many expat colleagues, if you want to find our relocation benefits, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://jobs.picnic.app/en/relocation&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
