&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position excluding 8% holiday pay is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€67.700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€91.500 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vinteden/senior-data-scientist-trust-safety-amsterdam-417890","tags":["Data Science & Analytics"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1792756513},{"slug":"engineering-manager-amsterdam-260715","company_name":"GreenFlux","title":"Engineering Manager","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">The company</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">Smart Electric Vehicle Charging Solutions. That’s the business we are in!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">GreenFlux offers a cloud-based charge point management SaaS (Software as a Service) solution. This software platform enables Charge Point Operators (CPOs) and e-Mobility Service Providers (eMSPs) to successfully launch their respective businesses. With its offering, GreenFlux plays a pivotal role in facilitating the uptake of electric vehicles and the renewable energy revolution.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">Our Development department is responsible for the technical design of new features, owns the architecture, and does technical operation. We are organised in agile end-to-end teams, working with well-defined and transparent processes. Our tech stack is centred around Microsoft .NET on Azure.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">To keep up with the rapid market and business expansion and to support the company’s dynamic growth, we are looking to bring an Engineering Manager to the team.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">The job</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW160586995 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">The Engineering Managers (internally referred to as Heads of Engineering) are responsible for the performance of our development teams and the quality of our platform. You will be responsible for line managing the engineers of up to three development teams, ensuring they have the right direction, skills, and support to deliver high-quality results. Besides this, you will contribute to improving our agile way of working and strengthening engineering practices throughout the Development department.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key result areas include:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Leadership and accountability:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You are the hierarchical manager of the engineers in your teams and are accountable for growing those teams to become autonomous and highly performing. You set clear expectations, provide regular feedback, and are accountable for individual and team performance. You actively identify and address performance issues and skill gaps, coaching and developing engineers to become more self-sufficient and effective.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Delivery and execution:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You take responsibility for ensuring your teams deliver high-quality software in a predictable and efficient manner. You proactively manage risks, dependencies, and impediments, taking action when delivery or quality is at risk and driving improvements where needed.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Technical quality:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You use your technical background to assess and challenge engineering decisions, ensuring that software solutions meet the required standards for quality, reliability, scalability, and maintainability. You work closely with engineers and technical leads to promote sound technical decisions and address technical debt</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Continuous improvement:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You drive improvements in engineering processes, ways of working, and the adoption of modern technologies, practices, and tools. You identify opportunities to increase efficiency, improve delivery performance, and strengthen engineering quality across teams.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Team development:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You build and maintain high-performing teams by ensuring the right balance of skills, experience, and perspectives. You proactively identify development needs, support professional growth, and foster a culture of ownership, collaboration, and continuous learning.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Quality and documentation:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You promote strong engineering standards, effective quality control, and clear technical documentation to support the long-term stability and maintainability of our platform.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW115915184 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW115915184 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Strategic contribution:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You contribute to setting the strategic direction of the Development department, translating broader objectives into concrete improvements and actions within your teams.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Requirements</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">We are looking for a strong and accountable engineering leader who combines a people-oriented approach with a clear focus on delivery, technical quality, and results. You empower your teams and create an environment where people take ownership of their work. You have a strong agile mindset without being dogmatic about tools and frameworks, and you know when to coach, challenge, or take decisive action to improve performance.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#121317">You have</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">3+ years of experience as an Engineering Manager, preferably in a tech scale-up or SaaS environment.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">A solid background in software engineering, with the technical expertise to evaluate engineering decisions and assess software quality, reliability, scalability, and maintainability.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Proven experience in leading engineering teams, setting clear expectations, managing performance, and addressing skill gaps through coaching, feedback, and development.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">A strong focus on delivery and execution, with the ability to take ownership of results, proactively manage risks, and drive improvements.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Extensive knowledge of software development processes, modern engineering practices, and agile ways of working.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the confidence to challenge decisions, provide constructive feedback, and collaborate with different stakeholder groups.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">The ability to think and act strategically while also translating plans into concrete actions and measurable improvements.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Fluency in English. Dutch is a plus.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">A drive for continuous learning and self-improvement.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW234532545 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">A sustainable mindset!</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Our offer</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">Working at GreenFlux means working in a dynamic, innovative, and informal organization, where new ideas and developments move quickly, and each day brings new opportunities and challenges. At one of the most inspiring locations in Amsterdam, you will have the chance to actively contribute to a sustainable future!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8" style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#121317">We are striving towards an international and inclusive team, so we also offer Visa sponsorship and relocation compensation to expats.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW234532545 BCX8"><span style="color:#121317">Join our revolution in mobility and energy!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/greenflux/engineering-manager-amsterdam-260715","tags":["IT Development"],"job_types":["Manager","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792756291},{"slug":"remote-seo-digital-marketing-specialist-netherlands-5151","company_name":"Pavago","title":"SEO & Digital Marketing Specialist","description":"<h2><strong>SEO &amp; Digital Marketing Specialist – Technical SEO, Google Ads &amp; Lead Generation | Remote</strong></h2><p><strong>Position Type:</strong> Full-Time, Remote<br> <strong>Working Hours:</strong> U.S. Business Hours<br> <strong>Experience Level:</strong> Mid-Level to Senior<br> <strong>Department:</strong> Digital Marketing / Growth Marketing</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p>At Pavago, one of our clients is hiring an experienced <strong>SEO &amp; Digital Marketing Specialist</strong> to develop, execute, and optimize digital marketing strategies that increase organic traffic, improve search rankings, generate qualified leads, and drive measurable business growth.</p><p>The ideal candidate has strong expertise in <strong>technical SEO, Google Ads, paid social advertising, content optimization, marketing analytics, and automation</strong>. This is a hands-on role requiring someone who can independently manage campaigns, identify growth opportunities, and turn marketing data into actionable strategies.</p><p>You’ll take ownership of organic search performance, paid advertising, website optimization, and lead generation while exploring emerging opportunities in <strong>AI-powered search optimization (AEO/GEO)</strong>.</p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></h2><h3><strong>SEO Strategy &amp; Optimization</strong></h3><ul><li>Develop and execute SEO strategies to improve organic visibility, keyword rankings, and website traffic.</li><li>Conduct keyword research, competitor analysis, and search intent analysis.</li><li>Perform technical SEO audits, addressing indexing, crawling, site architecture, page speed, and mobile performance.</li><li>Optimize meta titles, descriptions, headings, internal linking, URLs, and structured data.</li><li>Execute ethical link-building strategies and monitor search algorithm updates.</li><li>Optimize content for traditional search engines and AI-powered search experiences (AEO/GEO).</li></ul><h3><strong>Paid Advertising &amp; Lead Generation</strong></h3><ul><li>Plan, launch, and optimize campaigns across <strong>Google Ads, Meta Ads, and LinkedIn Ads</strong>.</li><li>Manage advertising budgets to improve lead quality, Cost per Lead (CPL), and Return on Ad Spend (ROAS).</li><li>Develop and optimize landing pages, lead capture forms, and conversion funnels.</li><li>Implement retargeting and remarketing campaigns.</li><li>Collaborate with sales teams to align marketing initiatives with revenue goals.</li></ul><h3><strong>Content Marketing &amp; Website Management</strong></h3><ul><li>Develop SEO-driven content strategies aligned with business objectives.</li><li>Create and optimize website copy, blog articles, and landing pages.</li><li>Manage website updates through <strong>WordPress, Webflow, or similar CMS platforms</strong>.</li><li>Collaborate with designers, developers, and content creators to improve website performance and user experience.</li></ul><h3><strong>Analytics, Reporting &amp; Optimization</strong></h3><ul><li>Monitor traffic, keyword rankings, conversions, and campaign performance using <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4), Google Search Console, and Google Tag Manager</strong>.</li><li>Build performance dashboards and provide actionable marketing reports.</li><li>Conduct A/B testing across landing pages, advertisements, and campaigns.</li><li>Analyze user behavior and identify opportunities to improve conversion rates.</li></ul><h3><strong>Marketing Automation &amp; CRM</strong></h3><ul><li>Manage email marketing campaigns, lead nurturing sequences, and automated workflows.</li><li>Work with platforms such as <strong>HubSpot, GoHighLevel, Salesforce, or ActiveCampaign</strong>.</li><li>Improve lead tracking, marketing attribution, and sales handoffs.</li><li>Maintain accurate campaign data and performance reporting.</li></ul><h2><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h2><ul><li><strong>3+ years of professional experience</strong> in SEO, digital marketing, or performance marketing.</li><li>Proven success improving organic rankings, website traffic, and qualified lead generation.</li><li>Strong knowledge of <strong>technical SEO, on-page SEO, off-page SEO, and content optimization</strong>.</li><li>Hands-on experience with <strong>GA4, Google Search Console, Google Tag Manager, SEMrush, Ahrefs, or similar tools</strong>.</li><li>Experience managing <strong>Google Ads and paid social media campaigns</strong>.</li><li>Familiarity with WordPress, Webflow, or other CMS platforms.</li><li>Understanding of conversion rate optimization (CRO), landing pages, and lead generation funnels.</li><li>Experience with CRM and marketing automation platforms.</li><li>Strong analytical skills and ability to translate data into actionable improvements.</li><li>Excellent written and verbal English communication skills.</li><li>Ability to independently manage multiple campaigns and meet deadlines.</li><li>Availability during <strong>U.S. Business Hours</strong>.</li></ul><h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></h2><ul><li>Experience with <strong>Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)</strong> and <strong>Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)</strong>.</li><li>Knowledge of local SEO and Google Business Profile optimization.</li><li>Familiarity with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and technical website improvements.</li><li>Experience in B2B marketing, SaaS, professional services, or lead-generation businesses.</li><li>Experience with Looker Studio and advanced marketing reporting.</li><li>Certifications in Google Ads, Google Analytics, HubSpot, or SEO.</li></ul><h2><strong>What Makes You a Strong Fit</strong></h2><ul><li>You take ownership of marketing performance and focus on measurable results.</li><li>You understand how SEO, paid advertising, content, and conversion optimization work together.</li><li>You can independently develop strategies, execute campaigns, and analyze performance.</li><li>You’re proactive about identifying growth opportunities and testing improvements.</li><li>You stay informed about search engine updates and emerging AI-powered marketing trends.</li><li>You communicate clearly and collaborate effectively with remote teams.</li></ul><h2><strong>What a Typical Day Looks Like</strong></h2><p>Your day may begin by reviewing <strong>GA4, Google Search Console, and advertising dashboards</strong> to evaluate traffic, keyword rankings, and lead generation performance. You’ll investigate SEO opportunities, optimize paid campaigns, update website content, or improve landing page conversions.</p><p>You may also configure marketing automation workflows, analyze campaign results, and collaborate with sales or development teams to implement improvements.</p><p><strong>In short:</strong> You’ll manage SEO, paid advertising, analytics, and marketing automation to generate qualified leads and drive measurable business growth.</p><h2><strong>Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)</strong></h2><p>Success in this role will be measured through:</p><ul><li><strong>Organic Traffic Growth:</strong> Increase qualified organic website traffic.</li><li><strong>Keyword Rankings:</strong> Improve rankings for high-intent commercial keywords.</li><li><strong>Lead Generation:</strong> Increase marketing-qualified leads from organic and paid channels.</li><li><strong>Conversion Rate:</strong> Improve website and landing page conversions.</li><li><strong>Cost per Lead (CPL):</strong> Optimize advertising spend and acquisition efficiency.</li><li><strong>Return on Ad Spend (ROAS):</strong> Improve paid campaign profitability.</li><li><strong>Technical SEO Health:</strong> Maintain indexing, crawling, and website performance.</li><li><strong>Marketing Attribution:</strong> Ensure accurate tracking of leads, conversions, and campaign results.</li></ul><h2><strong>Interview Process</strong></h2><ol><li>Initial Application</li><li><strong>Spark Hire One-Way Video Interview</strong></li><li>Recruiter Screening</li><li>Client Interview</li><li>Final Selection &amp; Onboarding</li></ol><h2><strong>Spark Hire Video Interview – Required</strong></h2><p>As part of the application process, <strong>all candidates are required to complete a one-way video interview through Spark Hire</strong>.</p><p>After completing the first step of your application, you’ll receive a <strong>Spark Hire invitation by email</strong> with instructions to record and submit your video responses.</p><p>Completion of the Spark Hire video is <strong>required to be considered for the next stage</strong>. Please check your inbox as well as your spam or junk folder for the invitation.</p><h2><strong>Apply Now</strong></h2><p>If you’re an experienced <strong>SEO Specialist, Digital Marketing Specialist, or Performance Marketing Professional</strong> with expertise in technical SEO, Google Ads, analytics, and lead generation, we’d love to hear from you.</p><p>Join a remote team where you can take ownership of digital marketing initiatives, optimize campaigns, and deliver measurable business results.</p><p><strong>#SEOSpecialist #DigitalMarketing #TechnicalSEO #GoogleAds #PerformanceMarketing #LeadGeneration #AEO #GEO #MarketingAutomation #RemoteMarketingJobs #RemoteJobs</strong></p><p><strong>#LI-AG1</strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/pavago/remote-seo-digital-marketing-specialist-netherlands-5151","tags":["Staffing and Recruiting","Remote"],"job_types":[],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1792747214},{"slug":"director-sales-nordics-eastern-europe-283804","company_name":"Pingidentity","title":"Director, Sales (Nordics & Eastern Europe)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it&#39;s not just something we provide our customers. It&#39;s something that inspires our company. People don&#39;t come here to join a culture that&#39;s built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html&quot;&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we&#39;re changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sales Director will be tasked with influencing and developing an energized, competitive, high impact sales team that is characterized by its ability to create differentiated value for our customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a seasoned leader from within the SaaS enterprise marketplace, with proven software solution selling combined with success in a fast growth business. This leader will be a model to drive the team in building extraordinary customer relationships and experiences, leveraging a strong teamwork approach, and cross matrix collaboration across all Ping functions. This role will demonstrate a depth of understanding when working alongside a partner community and posess a well-established customer and partner network in the Nordics &amp;amp; Eastern Europe regions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In order to acquire, develop and retain customer relationships and create a winning Ping business, this leader will be able to create and maintain a high-performance culture, that is grounded in data, transparency, accountability, and agility. The ideal candidate’s mindset should be customer-focused, people-oriented, open, passionate, and authentic.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creates, implements, measures and reviews a strategic or operational plan that drives achievement of business goals aligned to overall Ping strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses mechanisms such as territory planning, account plans, opportunity inspection, pipeline management, account reviews, forecast calls, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advises and coaches the sales team around how to position and articulate Ping Identity’s value proposition at enterprise customers, thus increasing the average deal size&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies and pursues opportunities to expand business activities within areas of responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages GSIs &amp;amp; other partners to help source, develop and progress business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plans and controls the expense associated with the area of responsibility even if not responsible for overall cost center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishes working relationships with external parties which supports the achievement of business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is conversant with Ping Identity’s systems and procedures and ensures effective use of and conformance to standard business practices and tools (i.e. SFDC – SalesForce.com)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates Ping Identity’s vision and aligns team and personal goals to achieve business results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides direction and guidance, mentoring and development of the field team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lives teamwork and promotes cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruits, builds and develops the team to deliver business results; Identifies, develops and promotes high potential employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommends and/or approves people-related decisions – hiring, promotions, merit increases, rewards &amp;amp; recognition, training initiatives, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives performance review and development planning process with annual and quarterly review meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has established multi-vertical C level contacts in large enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has an established partner/SI network and is used to working with partners on projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds relationships with customers (internal or external) as necessary providing customer escalation management as necessary for problem resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides support for customer relationship management as necessary and drives initiatives which result in improvement in customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives initiatives which result in improvement in customer satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
