 Stories &amp; Acceptance Criteria:</strong> Create and refine Epics, Features, and User Stories with clear scope, detailed acceptance criteria, dependencies, and relevant functional and non-functional requirements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Business Process Documentation:</strong> Prepare process flows (as-is/to-be), mockups, business rules, data mappings, impact assessments, and other supporting documentation as required.</p></li><li><p><strong>Microsoft Power Platform:</strong> Understand Power Apps (Canvas and Model-driven), Power BI, Power Pages, Dataverse, access structures, data models, solution architecture, and inbound/outbound data flows.</p></li><li><p><strong>Agile &amp; SAFe Delivery:</strong> Participate in PI Planning, backlog refinement, sprint planning, daily meetings, system demos, and other Agile/SAFe ceremonies.</p></li><li><p><strong>PI Preparation:</strong> Support pre-PI planning activities, identify knowledge gaps and dependencies, prepare refinement materials, and coordinate with relevant teams to ensure feature readiness.</p></li><li><p><strong>Definition of Ready &amp; Definition of Done:</strong> Ensure that User Stories meet the agreed Definition of Ready (DoR) before entering a sprint and contain the necessary information to support the Definition of Done (DoD).</p></li><li><p><strong>Technical &amp; Cross-Team Coordination:</strong> Collaborate with development leads, testers, Product Owners, and other teams to clarify technical feasibility, resolve dependencies, and maintain alignment on scope and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p><strong>User Acceptance Testing (UAT):</strong> Prepare UAT scenarios, use cases, and sample test data; coordinate end-user testing; collect and analyze feedback; and document decisions and follow-up backlog items.</p></li><li><p><strong>Delivery &amp; Release Support:</strong> Verify that delivered functionality meets business requirements, prepare sprint release notes, and ensure that documentation, user guidance, and training materials are updated.</p></li><li><p><strong>Documentation &amp; Traceability:</strong> Maintain centralized and accessible project documentation in tools such as SharePoint or Wiki, ensuring traceability from Epics and Features through User Stories, acceptance tests, and releases.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI-Assisted Analysis:</strong> Use AI capabilities such as Copilot, AI agents, and other relevant tools to support requirements gathering, process analysis, validation of assumptions, and initial solution ideation.</p></li><li><p><strong>Continuous Improvement:</strong> Identify opportunities to simplify business processes, improve requirements quality, and maintain a backlog buffer of approximately 1.5–2 sprints of ready User Stories.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Job requirments:</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>Proven experience as a <strong>Business Analyst</strong> in Agile/Scrum and SAFe environments.</p></li><li><p>Strong experience in requirements elicitation, stakeholder management, business process analysis, and documentation.</p></li><li><p>Practical knowledge of Microsoft Power Platform, including:</p><ul><li><p>Power Apps (Canvas and Model-driven apps)</p></li><li><p>Power BI</p></li><li><p>Power Pages</p></li><li><p>Microsoft Dataverse</p></li><li><p>Data models, access structures, and data integrations.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Experience defining and refining Epics, Features, User Stories, and detailed Acceptance Criteria.</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of backlog management, refinement sessions, sprint planning, and PI Planning.</p></li><li><p>Experience with business process modelling, process flows, mockups, business rules, data mappings, and impact assessments.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of functional and non-functional requirements, including performance, scalability, availability, security, auditability, and GDPR/privacy.</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Definition of Ready (DoR), Definition of Done (DoD), and requirements traceability.</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting UAT, including test scenario preparation, test data coordination, feedback analysis, and defect or backlog item management.</p></li><li><p>Ability to identify dependencies, clarify scope, assess gaps, and coordinate with technical teams and business stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with technical documentation, solution architecture, data models, APIs, and integration flows.</p></li><li><p>Experience using documentation and collaboration tools such as SharePoint, Wiki, and backlog management platforms.</p></li><li><p>Awareness of AI tools, including Copilot and AI agents, for requirements analysis, process improvement, and solution ideation.</p></li><li><p>Strong communication, analytical, facilitation, problem-solving, and organizational skills.</p></li><li><p>Ability to work collaboratively with cross-functional teams and manage multiple features and priorities in a structured delivery environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/almaviva-de-belgique/senior-business-analyst-deadline-03-11-2026-amsterdam-490409","tags":["Europe"],"job_types":["Mid","freelance"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792722670},{"slug":"meewerkstage-communicatie-rijssen-214846","company_name":"Voortman Steel Machinery","title":"Meewerkstage: Communicatie","description":"<h2>Wat ga je doen?</h2><p>Hoe zorg je ervoor dat 800+ collega’s wereldwijd weten wat er binnen Voortman speelt én zich betrokken voelen bij de organisatie? Met verschillende vestigingen, landen, afdelingen en groepen collega’s is dat een mooie communicatie-uitdaging. Want niet iedere doelgroep bereik je op dezelfde manier en niet ieder verhaal vertel je via hetzelfde kanaal.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p